export const reportHtml = "\n\n<header class=\"masthead\">\n  <div class=\"stamp\">\n    <span>Deepgrid Semi Pvt Ltd</span>\n    <span>Investor executive summary</span>\n    <span>Pre-Series A &middot; <b>&#8377;45 Cr equity</b></span>\n    <span>T-Hub, Hyderabad</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>One die, fifteen products</h1>\n  <p class=\"standfirst\">A six-chiplet 28&nbsp;nm automotive SoC, taped out in gated stages, sold as fifteen products into a market where the demand date is written into law. <strong>&#8377;1,128&nbsp;Cr of FY2032 revenue rests on one tapeout</strong> &mdash; which is the whole investment case, and the whole risk.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"figures\">\n    <div class=\"fig\"><span class=\"k\">Equity round</span><span class=\"v\">&#8377;45<em> Cr</em></span><span class=\"n\">$4.79M for 18.07% &middot; &#8377;204 Cr pre</span></div>\n    <div class=\"fig\"><span class=\"k\">FY2032 revenue</span><span class=\"v\">&#8377;1,128<em> Cr</em></span><span class=\"n\">from &#8377;1.7 Cr in FY2027</span></div>\n    <div class=\"fig\"><span class=\"k\">FY2032 gross margin</span><span class=\"v\">87.4<em>%</em></span><span class=\"n\">EBITDA &#8377;387.9 Cr &middot; 34.4%</span></div>\n    <div class=\"fig\"><span class=\"k\">Measured on silicon</span><span class=\"v\">40<em> fps</em></span><span class=\"n\">YOLOv11n live on an Artix-7 FPGA</span></div>\n    <div class=\"fig\"><span class=\"k\">Cash, June 2026</span><span class=\"v\">&#8377;2.5<em> L</em></span><span class=\"n\">bridge being arranged</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <figure class=\"plate\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"./images/figure-01.webp\" width=\"1500\" height=\"276\" alt=\"Photographs of the DeepGrid AD2 truck platform, radar and thermal detection output, the A100 compute box and M.2 module, and the D-HUMR humanoid robot\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n  <figcaption><span class=\"figno\">Figure 01</span>Built, not rendered &mdash; the AD2 truck platform, radar and thermal perception output, the A100 compute box and M.2 module, and the D-HUMR defence robot. <b>YOLOv11n runs at 40 fps on an Artix-7 200T today</b>, measured, not simulated.<span class=\"figsrc\">Source &middot; Information Memorandum, p.6 &mdash; reproduced, not redrawn</span></figcaption></figure>\n</header>\n\n\n<div class=\"summary\">\n  <div class=\"summary-in\">\n    <p class=\"lbl\">The summary, if you read nothing else</p>\n    <p class=\"verdict\">Deepgrid Semi is a one-chip company with fifteen ways to sell the same die. <em>The chip is real</em> &mdash; six RTL designs are tapeout-ready, a 130&nbsp;nm tapeout is already done, and the perception stack runs at 40&nbsp;fps on an FPGA today. <em>The demand is real</em> &mdash; India is writing ADAS into law for commercial vehicles, function by function, on dated deadlines. What is not yet reconciled is the schedule between them.</p>\n    <p class=\"verdict\">Qualified silicon lands <em>H1 2028</em>, after the last mandate date, and OEM design-in runs 18&ndash;30 months. So the next two years are an FPGA business sold through government and PSU channels &mdash; and that, not the &#8377;1,128&nbsp;Cr terminal year, is what this round actually underwrites.</p>\n    <div class=\"figures\">\n      <div class=\"fig\"><span class=\"k\">Equity round</span><span class=\"v\">&#8377;45<em> Cr</em></span><span class=\"n\">$4.79M for 18.07% &middot; &#8377;204 Cr pre-money</span></div>\n      <div class=\"fig\"><span class=\"k\">FY2032 revenue</span><span class=\"v\">&#8377;1,128<em> Cr</em></span><span class=\"n\">from &#8377;1.7 Cr in FY2027, FPGA-only</span></div>\n      <div class=\"fig\"><span class=\"k\">FY2032 gross margin</span><span class=\"v\">87.4<em>%</em></span><span class=\"n\">EBITDA positive from FY2028</span></div>\n      <div class=\"fig\"><span class=\"k\">Die cost at volume</span><span class=\"v\">$3.88</span><span class=\"n\">NRE breaks even at 174,908 chips</span></div>\n      <div class=\"fig\"><span class=\"k\">Cash, June 2026</span><span class=\"v\">&#8377;2.5<em> L</em></span><span class=\"n\">prior capital deployed, not banked</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <dl class=\"uw3\">\n    <div><dt>Underwrite this &mdash; 01</dt><dd><b>Two products carry 64% of revenue.</b> The truck kit and the smart mirror are one family sold to overlapping buyers. A certification delay hits &#8377;720&nbsp;Cr at once.</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Underwrite this &mdash; 02</dt><dd><b>The FPGA window, not the ASIC.</b> Nothing beyond FY2027&rsquo;s &#8377;1.7&nbsp;Cr happens without production silicon, and silicon arrives after every mandate date.</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Underwrite this &mdash; 03</dt><dd><b>Three headline claims fail the company&rsquo;s own controls.</b> The mandate date, the &#8377;1&nbsp;Cr defence revenue and the price comparison are all barred by its internal ledger &mdash; and printed anyway.</dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"askline\"><b>The ask.</b> Release capital against silicon, certification and paying customers. The $3.17M of tapeout NRE is already structured as four gates, and six of nine de-risking milestones are marked done before the round opens &mdash; so the forecast is the consequence of those gates, not the thing being funded.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"spine\">\n  <p class=\"lbl\">The argument in seven moves</p>\n  <ol>\n    <li><b>Demand is written into law</b><span>Five ADAS functions become mandatory on commercial vehicles across 2027&ndash;28. Roughly a million N2/N3 units a year fall in scope.</span></li>\n    <li><b>Foreign silicon prices India out</b><span>An imported ADAS module costs multiples of the kit price this market can pay, and no indigenous alternative exists at this stage.</span></li>\n    <li><b>So own the die</b><span>Six chiplets on one 57&nbsp;mm&sup2; part. Eleven sensor channels fused in 8.6&nbsp;ms of a 33.3&nbsp;ms frame.</span></li>\n    <li><b>The headroom is the portfolio</b><span>74% of the frame is unused, so fifteen products across four surfaces run on one mask and one firmware stack.</span></li>\n    <li class=\"turn\"><b>But the silicon arrives late</b><span>Qualified parts land H1 2028 &mdash; after every mandate date on the calendar &mdash; and design-in runs 18&ndash;30 months. This is the turn in the argument.</span></li>\n    <li><b>So the FPGA window is the strategy</b><span>Government and PSU units ship first, and the telemetry they generate is what makes the Tier-1 design-in winnable.</span></li>\n    <li><b>The round is priced against a &#8377;10.1 Cr trough</b><span>That is the whole margin of safety, and two dated obligations land inside it, funded nowhere.</span></li>\n  </ol>\n</div>\n\n<nav class=\"nav\" aria-label=\"Sections\">\n  <a href=\"#business\">I &nbsp;The business</a>\n  <a href=\"#technology\">II &nbsp;The technology</a>\n  <a href=\"#usecases\">III &nbsp;The use cases</a>\n  <a href=\"#choice\">IV &nbsp;The choice &amp; the case</a>\n  <a href=\"#numbers\">V &nbsp;The numbers and the risk</a>\n</nav>\n\n<div class=\"part\" id=\"business\">\n  <div class=\"part-head\"><span class=\"no\">Part I</span><h2>The business</h2><span class=\"cnt\">5 sections</span></div>\n<section>\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">The company</p>\n  <h2>An autonomous systems company that builds its own silicon</h2>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Deepgrid Semi sells complete, certified autonomy systems. It builds the six-chiplet die underneath them because owning the chip is the only way to ship those systems at a price the Indian market can pay.</p>\n  <p>Founded and led by <strong>Aravind Prasad G</strong> (20 years, multiple exits &mdash; Evolgence IT Solutions, Deepgrid Datacentre, Evolgence Energy), with <strong>Ayaz Khan</strong> as silicon architecture lead. Incorporated in Telangana (CIN U62099TS2024PTC183631), operating from T-Hub Phase 2, Knowledge City, Hyderabad. Thirty-four people today, <span class=\"num\">541</span> in the FY2032 plan. Angels are domain operators, including DFT and semiconductor engineers backing the company personally.</p>\n  <p>The order of markets is deliberate: <strong>commercial fleets</strong> are the mandate wedge and are live now; <strong>OEM design-in</strong> is the platform prize; <strong>defence and robotics</strong> is optionality on the same silicon that is already earning revenue. About <strong>88% of planned revenue is systems and products</strong>; roughly 5% is merchant silicon.</p>\n  <figure class=\"plate\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"./images/figure-02.webp\" width=\"1500\" height=\"366\" alt=\"Flow diagram: tapeout to silicon, branching to sensors and compute, converging on systems, then AI software, ending at safer roads and revenue\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n  <figcaption><span class=\"figno\">Figure 02</span>One tapeout seeds four business units. Bare silicon feeds sensors and compute; those fuse into systems; software sits on top. <b>The company&rsquo;s own cascade &mdash; and the first place its two totals diverge</b> (see Underwriting).<span class=\"figsrc\">Source &middot; Information Memorandum, p.5 &mdash; reproduced, not redrawn</span></figcaption></figure>\n</section><section>\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">Why now</p>\n  <h2>The demand is legislated, not forecast</h2>\n  <p>India is putting ADAS into law for commercial vehicles function by function, each with its own standard and its own date. Read at the standards level &mdash; the version that survives diligence &mdash; the schedule is this: <strong>AEBS</strong> (AIS-162, CMVR 96(12)) binds new models 1 Jan 2027 and all models 1 Oct 2027; <strong>drowsiness, blind-spot, moving-off and lane-departure warning</strong> (AIS-184/186/187/188, CMVR 125Q and 98(6)) bind new models 1 Oct 2027 and all models 1 Jan 2028. The financial model sizes the reachable pool at <span class=\"num\">~500k</span> new N2/N3 units a year plus a <span class=\"num\">~500k</span> retrofit pool &mdash; <strong>1.0M units</strong>.</p>\n  <p><strong>Four functions arriving on one clock is the commercial fact that matters.</strong> Every CV maker must source drowsiness, blind-spot, moving-off and lane-departure together, so a supplier that carries more than one of the four from a single perception core is materially easier to nominate than four separate suppliers. That, rather than any single function, is the design-in argument.</p>\n  <div class=\"figures\">\n    <div class=\"fig\"><span class=\"k\">Road fatalities / yr</span><span class=\"v\">168,000</span><span class=\"n\">60%+ addressable by ADAS intervention</span></div>\n    <div class=\"fig\"><span class=\"k\">ADAS penetration</span><span class=\"v\">&lt;5<em>%</em></span><span class=\"n\">across 70M vehicles &mdash; lowest of any major market</span></div>\n    <div class=\"fig\"><span class=\"k\">Mandated pool</span><span class=\"v\">1.0<em>M</em></span><span class=\"n\">N2/N3 units/yr, new + retrofit (model basis)</span></div>\n    <div class=\"fig\"><span class=\"k\">Indigenous alternatives</span><span class=\"v\">0</span><span class=\"n\">no Indian ADAS chipset at this stage of development</span></div>\n  </div>\n  <p>Three further rules stack on top of the truck mandate. <strong>AIS-140</strong> requires GPS and driver-behaviour monitoring on commercial fleets &mdash; the S100 chiplet carries that telematics interface natively, in every kit, at no added cost. <strong>AIS-004</strong> puts LDWS, FCWS and LKAS on all new M-category vehicles, creating aftermarket retrofit pull for the &#8377;50,000 mirror. And post-2022 supply fragility has Indian OEMs actively seeking a domestic chip partner.</p>\n</section><section>\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">The product ladder</p>\n  <h2>&#8377;50,000 to &#8377;4 lakh, one common platform</h2>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Five configurations of the same silicon, from passive alerts to full driverless &mdash; and one upgrade path that keeps the hardware already sold.</p>\n  <figure class=\"plate\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"./images/figure-03.webp\" width=\"1600\" height=\"609\" alt=\"Comparison table of the AD0 to AD4 product family with prices, sensor sets, SaaS rates and gross margins\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n  <figcaption><span class=\"figno\">Figure 03</span>AD0 passive alerts &rarr; AD1 geofenced L4 &rarr; <b>AD2, the primary wedge</b> &rarr; AD3 conditional &rarr; AD4 full autonomy. ASIC gross margin runs 80&ndash;84% across the whole ladder; the FPGA column is what ships today. AD0&rarr;AD2 upgrade is &#8377;1.60L, AD2&rarr;AD3 is &#8377;1.20L.<span class=\"figsrc\">Source &middot; Information Memorandum, p.13 &mdash; reproduced, not redrawn</span></figcaption></figure>\n  <p>Recurring revenue sits on top of every rung: SaaS at &#8377;5K&ndash;&#8377;25K per vehicle per year, Autonomous Truck DaaS at <strong>&#8377;2.5L/truck/yr (93% GM)</strong>, seaport AGV fleet ops at <strong>&#8377;45.3L/AGV/yr (92% GM)</strong>, and fleet-health SaaS through the H100 wearable at &#8377;8L/truck/yr. The plan has recurring revenue reaching <span class=\"num\">&#8377;116 Cr</span> by FY2032.</p>\n</section><section>\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">The portfolio</p>\n  <h2>Six buyer routes off one bill of materials</h2>\n  <p>The fifteen revenue lines reach market through genuinely different procurement motions &mdash; which is what keeps the concentration risk from being total.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"cases\">\n    <div class=\"case\">\n      <div class=\"case-video-box\">\n        <video src=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/truck.mp4\" poster=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/truck-poster.png\" controls preload=\"none\" playsinline style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 6px; background: #000; display: block;\"></video>\n        <div class=\"case-video-overlay\">\n          <div class=\"play-btn-circle\"><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg></div>\n          <span class=\"play-btn-label\">Play AD2 Smart Truck Simulation</span>\n        </div>\n        <span class=\"video-badge\"><svg width=\"10\" height=\"10\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Video & Audio</span>\n      </div>\n      <span class=\"tag\">Mandate wedge</span><h3>AD2 Smart Truck kit</h3><p>Six cameras, two radars, LiDAR and drive-by-wire on an N2/N3 truck, certified to AIS-162/188. Fleet ROI under two years on insurance premium reduction alone.</p><div class=\"meta\">&#8377;2.5L &middot; 18,000 units FY32<br><b>&#8377;450 Cr</b> &middot; 1.8% of the 1.0M mandated pool</div></div>\n    <div class=\"case\">\n      <div class=\"case-video-box\">\n        <video src=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/ddrive.mp4\" poster=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/ddrive-poster.png\" controls preload=\"none\" playsinline style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 6px; background: #000; display: block;\"></video>\n        <div class=\"case-video-overlay\">\n          <div class=\"play-btn-circle\"><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg></div>\n          <span class=\"play-btn-label\">Play AD0 Smart Mirror Simulation</span>\n        </div>\n        <span class=\"video-badge\"><svg width=\"10\" height=\"10\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Video & Audio</span>\n      </div>\n      <span class=\"tag\">Already selling</span><h3>AD0 Smart Mirror</h3><p>Replacement mirror with display, four body cameras, a loom and a 15-minute fitment. No mandate applies &mdash; it sells as an accessory through fitment shops today, and builds the channel the harder products inherit.</p><div class=\"meta\">&#8377;50,000 &middot; 54,000 units FY32<br><b>&#8377;270 Cr</b> &middot; 0.9% of a $3.09B pool</div></div>\n    <div class=\"case\">\n      <div class=\"case-video-box\">\n        <video src=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/forklift.mp4\" poster=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/forklift-poster.png\" controls preload=\"none\" playsinline style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 6px; background: #000; display: block;\"></video>\n        <div class=\"case-video-overlay\">\n          <div class=\"play-btn-circle\"><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg></div>\n          <span class=\"play-btn-label\">Play AD1 Autonomous AMR Simulation</span>\n        </div>\n        <span class=\"video-badge\"><svg width=\"10\" height=\"10\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Video & Audio</span>\n      </div>\n      <span class=\"tag\">Level 4, shipping early</span><h3>AD1 Indoor autonomy</h3><p>Forklifts and tugs a site already owns, retrofitted to drive themselves. Geofenced, &le;25&nbsp;km/h, &plusmn;5&nbsp;cm obstacle stop. No homologation inside a private site, so L4 ships years before it is legal on a road.</p><div class=\"meta\">&#8377;1L &middot; 4,200 units FY32<br><b>&#8377;42 Cr</b> &middot; the technical proof point</div></div>\n    <div class=\"case\">\n      <div class=\"case-video-box\">\n        <video src=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/yard.mp4\" poster=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/yard-poster.png\" controls preload=\"none\" playsinline style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 6px; background: #000; display: block;\"></video>\n        <div class=\"case-video-overlay\">\n          <div class=\"play-btn-circle\"><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg></div>\n          <span class=\"play-btn-label\">Play Seaport AGV Fleet Ops Simulation</span>\n        </div>\n        <span class=\"video-badge\"><svg width=\"10\" height=\"10\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Video & Audio</span>\n      </div>\n      <span class=\"tag\">Live order</span><h3>Seaport AGV</h3><p>The autonomous vehicle layer of container-terminal automation, sold as fleet operations rather than hardware. Electric, no fuel, 92% gross margin on the ops contract.</p><div class=\"meta\">&#8377;45.3L/AGV/yr &middot; 50 units FY32<br><b>&#8377;22.65 Cr</b> &middot; live at Vizag Container Terminal</div></div>\n    <div class=\"case\">\n      <div class=\"case-video-box\">\n        <video src=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/sentinel.mp4\" poster=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/sentinel-poster.png\" controls preload=\"none\" playsinline style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 6px; background: #000; display: block;\"></video>\n        <div class=\"case-video-overlay\">\n          <div class=\"play-btn-circle\"><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg></div>\n          <span class=\"play-btn-label\">Play D-HUMR Sovereign Defence Robot Simulation</span>\n        </div>\n        <span class=\"video-badge\"><svg width=\"10\" height=\"10\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Video & Audio</span>\n      </div>\n      <span class=\"tag\">Revenue received</span><h3>D-HUMR defence</h3><p>Humanoid, UGV and drone compute on the D100 secure enclave &mdash; AES-256, lockstep RISC-V, ECC SRAM. A sovereign procurement route that does not depend on the automotive mandate at all.</p><div class=\"meta\">&#8377;20L &middot; 150 units FY32<br><b>&#8377;30 Cr</b> &middot; &#8377;23.01L delivered, MCEME pipeline active</div></div>\n    <div class=\"case\">\n      <div class=\"case-video-box\">\n        <video src=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/cube.mp4\" poster=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/cube-poster.png\" controls preload=\"none\" playsinline style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 6px; background: #000; display: block;\"></video>\n        <div class=\"case-video-overlay\">\n          <div class=\"play-btn-circle\"><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg></div>\n          <span class=\"play-btn-label\">Play T100 Licensable Core Architecture Simulation</span>\n        </div>\n        <span class=\"video-badge\"><svg width=\"10\" height=\"10\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Video & Audio</span>\n      </div>\n      <span class=\"tag\">Zero bill of materials</span><h3>T100 AI licence</h3><p>The core itself, licensed to an OEM rather than sold as a part. Starts FY2029 because a licence needs a track record &mdash; the only line in the plan with no BOM whatsoever.</p><div class=\"meta\">&#8377;1 Cr/licence &middot; 50 FY32<br><b>&#8377;50 Cr</b> &middot; 94% gross margin</div></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"tablewrap\">\n    <table>\n      <thead><tr><th>FY2032 revenue line</th><th class=\"n\">ASP &#8377;</th><th class=\"n\">Units</th><th class=\"n\">&#8377; Cr</th><th>Sized demand pool</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr class=\"grp\"><td colspan=\"5\">Road autonomy &mdash; &#8377;762 Cr &middot; 67.5%</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>AD2 Smart Truck kit</td><td class=\"n\">2,50,000</td><td class=\"n\">18,000</td><td class=\"n\">450.00</td><td>1.0M mandated N2/N3, new + retrofit</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>AD0 Smart Mirror</td><td class=\"n\">50,000</td><td class=\"n\">54,000</td><td class=\"n\">270.00</td><td>360&deg; surround-view, $3.09B (2025)</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>AD1 Indoor L4 kit</td><td class=\"n\">1,00,000</td><td class=\"n\">4,200</td><td class=\"n\">42.00</td><td>Warehouse autonomy, in $4.8B edge-AI</td></tr>\n        <tr class=\"grp\"><td colspan=\"5\">Silicon &amp; compute &mdash; &#8377;194.3 Cr &middot; 17.2%</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Chipset OEM (ASIC die)</td><td class=\"n\">18,000</td><td class=\"n\">30,000</td><td class=\"n\">54.00</td><td>India ADAS chip, $2.29B (2024)</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>T100 AI licence</td><td class=\"n\">1,00,00,000</td><td class=\"n\">50</td><td class=\"n\">50.00</td><td>IP licensing, 90%+ margin</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>A100 compute box 4ch (PCIe)</td><td class=\"n\">3,00,000</td><td class=\"n\">1,200</td><td class=\"n\">36.00</td><td rowspan=\"3\">Automotive edge-AI modules, $4.8B (2025)</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>A100 compute box 2ch</td><td class=\"n\">1,60,000</td><td class=\"n\">1,800</td><td class=\"n\">28.80</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>A100 compute box 1ch (M.2)</td><td class=\"n\">85,000</td><td class=\"n\">3,000</td><td class=\"n\">25.50</td></tr>\n        <tr class=\"grp\"><td colspan=\"5\">Fleet &amp; mobility &mdash; &#8377;88.65 Cr &middot; 7.9%</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Autonomous TaaS</td><td class=\"n\">66,00,000</td><td class=\"n\">100</td><td class=\"n\">66.00</td><td>India trucking, 0.6&ndash;0.8M units/yr</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Seaport AGV</td><td class=\"n\">45,30,000</td><td class=\"n\">50</td><td class=\"n\">22.65</td><td>Container terminals, $10.95B (2024)</td></tr>\n        <tr class=\"grp\"><td colspan=\"5\">Sensors &amp; robotics &mdash; &#8377;83.5 Cr &middot; 7.4%</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Defence D-HUMR</td><td class=\"n\">20,00,000</td><td class=\"n\">150</td><td class=\"n\">30.00</td><td>Indian Army UGV / robotics</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>D100 drone SoC kit</td><td class=\"n\">5,00,000</td><td class=\"n\">400</td><td class=\"n\">20.00</td><td>India defence + commercial drone SoC</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Thermal camera</td><td class=\"n\">50,000</td><td class=\"n\">3,200</td><td class=\"n\">16.00</td><td>Automotive thermal, $1.68B (2025)</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>H100 driver-monitor wearable</td><td class=\"n\">5,000</td><td class=\"n\">20,000</td><td class=\"n\">10.00</td><td>DDAWS mandate + global DMS</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>4D radar pod</td><td class=\"n\">25,000</td><td class=\"n\">3,000</td><td class=\"n\">7.50</td><td>4D imaging radar, $2.75B (2025)</td></tr>\n        <tr class=\"total\"><td>Total</td><td class=\"n\">&mdash;</td><td class=\"n\">1,38,150</td><td class=\"n\">1,128.45</td><td>No line exceeds 2% of its own pool</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"chart\">\n    <p class=\"ch-title\">Original analysis &middot; revenue concentration, FY2032</p>\n    <p class=\"ch-sub\">All fifteen lines at the same scale, sorted. The concentration the plan discloses in a sentence, drawn.</p>\n    <div class=\"conc\">\n      <div class=\"cc-row top\"><span class=\"nm\">AD2 Smart Truck kit</span><span class=\"tr\"><span class=\"fl\" style=\"width:100.0%\"></span></span><span class=\"vv\">450.0</span></div>\n      <div class=\"cc-row top\"><span class=\"nm\">AD0 Smart Mirror</span><span class=\"tr\"><span class=\"fl\" style=\"width:60.0%\"></span></span><span class=\"vv\">270.0</span></div>\n      <div class=\"cc-cut\"><span>&#8595;&nbsp; &#8377;720 Cr &mdash; 63.8% of FY2032 revenue sits above this line, in two products sold to overlapping buyers</span></div>\n      <div class=\"cc-row\"><span class=\"nm\">Autonomous TaaS</span><span class=\"tr\"><span class=\"fl\" style=\"width:14.7%\"></span></span><span class=\"vv\">66.0</span></div>\n      <div class=\"cc-row\"><span class=\"nm\">Chipset OEM die</span><span class=\"tr\"><span class=\"fl\" style=\"width:12.0%\"></span></span><span class=\"vv\">54.0</span></div>\n      <div class=\"cc-row\"><span class=\"nm\">T100 AI licence</span><span class=\"tr\"><span class=\"fl\" style=\"width:11.1%\"></span></span><span class=\"vv\">50.0</span></div>\n      <div class=\"cc-row\"><span class=\"nm\">AD1 Indoor L4 kit</span><span class=\"tr\"><span class=\"fl\" style=\"width:9.3%\"></span></span><span class=\"vv\">42.0</span></div>\n      <div class=\"cc-row\"><span class=\"nm\">A100 box 4ch</span><span class=\"tr\"><span class=\"fl\" style=\"width:8.0%\"></span></span><span class=\"vv\">36.0</span></div>\n      <div class=\"cc-row\"><span class=\"nm\">Defence D-HUMR</span><span class=\"tr\"><span class=\"fl\" style=\"width:6.7%\"></span></span><span class=\"vv\">30.0</span></div>\n      <div class=\"cc-row\"><span class=\"nm\">A100 box 2ch</span><span class=\"tr\"><span class=\"fl\" style=\"width:6.4%\"></span></span><span class=\"vv\">28.8</span></div>\n      <div class=\"cc-row\"><span class=\"nm\">A100 box 1ch</span><span class=\"tr\"><span class=\"fl\" style=\"width:5.7%\"></span></span><span class=\"vv\">25.5</span></div>\n      <div class=\"cc-row\"><span class=\"nm\">Seaport AGV</span><span class=\"tr\"><span class=\"fl\" style=\"width:5.0%\"></span></span><span class=\"vv\">22.6</span></div>\n      <div class=\"cc-row\"><span class=\"nm\">D100 drone SoC kit</span><span class=\"tr\"><span class=\"fl\" style=\"width:4.4%\"></span></span><span class=\"vv\">20.0</span></div>\n      <div class=\"cc-row\"><span class=\"nm\">Thermal camera</span><span class=\"tr\"><span class=\"fl\" style=\"width:3.6%\"></span></span><span class=\"vv\">16.0</span></div>\n      <div class=\"cc-row\"><span class=\"nm\">H100 wearable</span><span class=\"tr\"><span class=\"fl\" style=\"width:2.2%\"></span></span><span class=\"vv\">10.0</span></div>\n      <div class=\"cc-row\"><span class=\"nm\">4D radar pod</span><span class=\"tr\"><span class=\"fl\" style=\"width:1.7%\"></span></span><span class=\"vv\">7.5</span></div>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"ch-note\">The thirteen lines below the cut total <b>&#8377;408.45 Cr</b> &mdash; less than the truck kit alone. Diversification across four surfaces is real in engineering terms and thin in revenue terms, which is why the concentration flag sits first in the underwriting list.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>Read the capture percentages as runway rather than ceiling: most pools above are <strong>global</strong> while the near-term serviceable market is the India slice. One caveat is stated rather than hidden &mdash; the seaport pool is total port automation including cranes and software, and Deepgrid sells only the vehicle layer.</p>\n</section><section>\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">The people</p>\n  <h2>A commercial founder and a standing silicon architect</h2>\n  <figure class=\"plate\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"./images/figure-04.webp\" width=\"1500\" height=\"384\" alt=\"Leadership profiles for the founder-CEO and CTO plus three board officers\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n  <figcaption><span class=\"figno\">Figure 04</span>Founder-CEO with 20 years and multiple exits; CTO who authored the R100 radar RTL and leads the 15-patent filing. Board carries an independent director and a virtual CFO ahead of the raise. <b>The CTO is not yet full-time</b> &mdash; the plan has that changing by Q1 FY28 (see Underwriting).<span class=\"figsrc\">Source &middot; Information Memorandum, p.29 &mdash; reproduced, not redrawn</span></figcaption></figure>\n  <p>R&amp;D sits under named academic supervision: <strong>Dr. Ramesh Patel</strong> and <strong>Dr. M.V. Kartikeyan</strong> (IIT Tirupati, ANRF MAHA Drones secure-SDR consortium), <strong>Prof. C. Krishna Mohan</strong> (IIT Hyderabad, VIGIL lab &mdash; intelligent transportation and real-time edge AI), and <strong>Dr. K.T. Satyajith</strong> (IMJ Institute of Research). The company&rsquo;s own note says each advisor&rsquo;s formal engagement status should be confirmed before the data room opens.</p>\n</section>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"part\" id=\"technology\">\n  <div class=\"part-head\"><span class=\"no\">Part II</span><h2>The technology</h2><span class=\"cnt\">4 sections</span></div>\n<section>\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">The silicon</p>\n  <h2>Six chiplets, one 57&nbsp;mm&sup2; die, six independent revenue lines</h2>\n  <p class=\"lead\">This is the asset the round buys. Each chiplet is a separate business, and replicating the set would take six tapeouts.</p>\n  <figure class=\"plate\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"./images/figure-05.webp\" width=\"1600\" height=\"740\" alt=\"Table of the six chiplets on the 57.1 square millimetre combo die with their functions and specifications\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n  \n    <div class=\"case-video-box\" style=\"margin: 10px 14px 14px; border-radius: 6px; max-width: 720px;\">\n      <video src=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/computebox.mp4\" poster=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/computebox-poster.png\" controls preload=\"none\" playsinline style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 6px; background: #000; display: block;\"></video>\n      <div class=\"case-video-overlay\">\n        <div class=\"play-btn-circle\"><svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg></div>\n        <span class=\"play-btn-label\">Play 6-Chiplet Die Architecture Simulation</span>\n      </div>\n      <span class=\"video-badge\"><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Video & Audio</span>\n    </div>\n    <figcaption><span class=\"figno\">Figure 05</span>A100 compute, R100 radar DSP, T100 edge AI, D100 defence secure compute, S100 vehicle gateway, H100 health AI &mdash; on one TSMC 28&nbsp;nm HPC+ die. <b>R100 eliminates the TI AWR2243 entirely in RTL</b>; D100 has already earned &#8377;1 Cr of institutional defence revenue.<span class=\"figsrc\">Source &middot; Information Memorandum, p.15 &mdash; reproduced, not redrawn</span></figcaption></figure>\n\n  <div class=\"budget\">\n    <div class=\"budget-head\"><span class=\"t\">One 30&nbsp;fps frame &middot; 33.3&nbsp;ms</span><span class=\"r\">8.6&nbsp;ms used &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; 24.7&nbsp;ms free</span></div>\n    <div class=\"bar\"><div class=\"used\">8.6 ms &mdash; 11-channel fusion</div><div class=\"free\">74% headroom &rarr; every other product runs here</div></div>\n    <p class=\"budget-note\">32,768 MACs at 600&nbsp;MHz gives a <em>derived</em> 39.3 TOPS INT8 &mdash; architecture arithmetic, not a silicon measurement &mdash; with 102.4&nbsp;GB/s of LPDDR5 bandwidth. The headroom is the product strategy: a drone stack, a wearable, a port AGV and a licensable core all fit inside the frame the truck kit leaves empty. PrimeSoC returned <b>FEASIBLE</b> on the architecture in March 2026.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  \n    <figure class=\"plate dark\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"./images/figure-06.webp\" width=\"1300\" height=\"856\" alt=\"Diagram contrasting a flat 8 by 8 activation slab with an 8 by 8 by 8 systolic cube retiring one K-slice per cycle\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n    \n    <div class=\"case-video-box\" style=\"margin: 10px 14px 14px; border-radius: 6px; max-width: 720px;\">\n      <video src=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/cube.mp4\" poster=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/cube-poster.png\" controls preload=\"none\" playsinline style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 6px; background: #000; display: block;\"></video>\n      <div class=\"case-video-overlay\">\n        <div class=\"play-btn-circle\"><svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg></div>\n        <span class=\"play-btn-label\">Play 8x8x8 3D Systolic Cube Simulation</span>\n      </div>\n      <span class=\"video-badge\"><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Video & Audio</span>\n    </div>\n    <figcaption><span class=\"figno\">Figure 06</span>The architectural claim, in one picture: a flat 8&times;8 array needs eight cycles to consume K. The 8&times;8&times;8 cube retires one K-slice <b>every cycle</b>. 64 cubes &times; 512 MACs = 32,768 at 600&nbsp;MHz.<span class=\"figsrc\">Source &middot; Information Memorandum, p.12 &mdash; reproduced, not redrawn</span></figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"plate dark\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"./images/figure-07.webp\" width=\"1500\" height=\"564\" alt=\"Diagram of eleven sensor channels feeding the in-cab compute box and producing AD2 perception output in 8.6 milliseconds\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n    <figcaption><span class=\"figno\">Figure 07</span>Eleven channels in, AD2 perception out, in 8.6&nbsp;ms: <b>7 RGB + 2 thermal + front/rear 4D 77&nbsp;GHz radar</b>. The AD2 kit itself is specified at six cameras; the compute box ingests eleven channels.<span class=\"figsrc\">Source &middot; Information Memorandum, p.10 &mdash; reproduced, not redrawn</span></figcaption></figure>\n\n  <p>Two claims underneath that are worth separating from the TOPS number, because they are the ones competitors cannot patch around. <strong>Batch-dispatch firmware (Patent 1)</strong> decouples inference from RISC-V host supervision, keeping the ALU active far longer per cycle &mdash; the company&rsquo;s answer to why headline TOPS on competing parts does not translate into delivered frames. And the <strong>R100&rsquo;s 12-bit native radar ADC</strong> preserves dynamic range that every competitor re-quantises to INT16, which is what buys detection sensitivity in monsoon and fog.</p>\n</section><section>\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">What it sees</p>\n  <h2>Two retrofit mirror towers, and no blind spot left on the vehicle</h2>\n  <p>The physical product is a pair of replacement mirror towers plus in-cab cameras and front/rear 77&nbsp;GHz radar. It installs in 15&ndash;35 minutes, needs no separate sensor sourcing, and the same mirror is reused at every rung of the upgrade ladder &mdash; which is where the customer-retention argument comes from: switching away means losing the India-trained model.</p>\n  \n    <figure class=\"plate dark\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"./images/figure-08.webp\" width=\"1000\" height=\"965\" alt=\"Overhead diagram of an N3 truck showing mirror-tower camera and radar coverage detecting an animal and a cyclist\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n    \n    <div class=\"case-video-box\" style=\"margin: 10px 14px 14px; border-radius: 6px; max-width: 720px;\">\n      <video src=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/truck.mp4\" poster=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/truck-poster.png\" controls preload=\"none\" playsinline style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 6px; background: #000; display: block;\"></video>\n      <div class=\"case-video-overlay\">\n        <div class=\"play-btn-circle\"><svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg></div>\n        <span class=\"play-btn-label\">Play Smart Mirror Tower Surround & Perception Video</span>\n      </div>\n      <span class=\"video-badge\"><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Video & Audio</span>\n    </div>\n    <figcaption><span class=\"figno\">Figure 08</span>Full surround coverage with <b>animal and cyclist detection in adverse conditions</b> &mdash; cattle, three-wheelers and unmarked lanes are exactly what European and US-trained models fail on.<span class=\"figsrc\">Source &middot; Information Memorandum, p.11 &mdash; reproduced, not redrawn</span></figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"plate\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"./images/figure-09.webp\" width=\"1400\" height=\"411\" alt=\"Head-to-head compliance table comparing DeepGrid A100 against Huawei, Mobileye, NVIDIA and Texas Instruments parts\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n    <figcaption><span class=\"figno\">Figure 09</span>The head-to-head the company puts forward: India-trained AI, AIS-004 native, sub-&#8377;4L kit, domestic IP, 12-bit radar. <b>Foreign parts cannot be software-patched to Indian conditions</b> &mdash; that needs Indian data, which needs being in the market first.<span class=\"figsrc\">Source &middot; Information Memorandum, p.20 &mdash; reproduced, not redrawn</span></figcaption></figure>\n</section><section>\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">Proof of execution</p>\n  <h2>Concept through validated silicon &mdash; what is already done</h2>\n  <figure class=\"plate\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"./images/figure-10.webp\" width=\"1600\" height=\"301\" alt=\"Timeline of nine de-risking milestones, six marked done, one contracted and two dated\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n  \n    <div class=\"case-video-box\" style=\"margin: 10px 14px 14px; border-radius: 6px; max-width: 720px;\">\n      <video src=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/roadmap.mp4\" poster=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/roadmap-poster.png\" controls preload=\"none\" playsinline style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 6px; background: #000; display: block;\"></video>\n      <div class=\"case-video-overlay\">\n        <div class=\"play-btn-circle\"><svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg></div>\n        <span class=\"play-btn-label\">Play Silicon Execution Roadmap Simulation</span>\n      </div>\n      <span class=\"video-badge\"><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Video & Audio</span>\n    </div>\n    <figcaption><span class=\"figno\">Figure 10</span>Six milestones marked DONE before the round opens, one contracted, and two dated. <b>This is the difference between a chip plan and a chip company</b> &mdash; the architecture has already been through a 130&nbsp;nm tapeout and an FPGA validation cycle.<span class=\"figsrc\">Source &middot; Information Memorandum, p.18 &mdash; reproduced, not redrawn</span></figcaption></figure>\n  <ul class=\"traction\">\n    <li><span class=\"amt\">Revenue</span><span class=\"desc\"><b>Institutional defence revenue earned on FPGA hardware</b> before ASIC exists. The memorandum states &#8377;1 Cr; the company&rsquo;s own claim controls substantiate <b>&#8377;23.01L delivered</b> with &#8377;78.39L at L1 stage rather than awarded &mdash; and in a separate legal entity. Use the delivered figure (see Underwriting).</span></li>\n    <li><span class=\"amt\">Measured</span><span class=\"desc\"><b>YOLOv11n at 40 fps on an Artix-7 200T</b> &mdash; 3.97M parameters, 263 layers, 80 classes, 24.8&nbsp;ms latency, at full L2+ ADAS spec. Not simulated.</span></li>\n    <li><span class=\"amt\">Silicon</span><span class=\"desc\"><b>Six RTL designs tapeout-ready</b> and a prior 130&nbsp;nm tapeout completed at SkyWater. R100 radar RTL replaces the TI AWR2243 DSP entirely.</span></li>\n    <li><span class=\"amt\">IP</span><span class=\"desc\"><b>15 provisional patents filed March 2026</b> (IN2026/DGR/001&ndash;015), covering batch-dispatch firmware, 12-bit native radar and the health processor.</span></li>\n    <li><span class=\"amt\">Foundry</span><span class=\"desc\"><b>Muse/GSME MPW contracted</b> &mdash; ~$630K shuttle, 79-day fab cycle, 96.7% predicted yield. PrimeSoC feasibility reports and the RTL&rarr;GDS physical design plan are filed.</span></li>\n    <li><span class=\"amt\">Supply chain</span><span class=\"desc\"><b>Manufacturing partners engaged and contracted</b> &mdash; EmbeddedIoT (Hyderabad) for PCBA and QFN-128 packaging, Sulakshna for 6-layer automotive PCBs.</span></li>\n  </ul>\n</section><section>\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">Far horizon</p>\n  <h2>The option the business buys you, deliberately not funded by this round</h2>\n  <p>SoC4-A is the next-generation part: 1,024 tiles on a finer node, packaged four to a 4U liquid-cooled chassis for <strong>16.76 PFLOPS FP4 peak</strong> and ~12 PFLOPS sustained at 1,120&nbsp;W, with 256&nbsp;GB of LPDDR5X. The pitch is sovereign AI inference &mdash; on-premise compute for Indian and GCC government, telecom and BFSI buyers whose data cannot leave the jurisdiction &mdash; plus robotaxi fleet compute and telecom edge.</p>\n  <div class=\"plates2\">\n    <figure class=\"plate\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"./images/figure-11.webp\" width=\"760\" height=\"488\" alt=\"Render of the MicroDC-A1 4U rack-mount chassis holding four SoC4-A chips with coolant pump and network module\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n    \n    <div class=\"case-video-box\" style=\"margin: 10px 14px 14px; border-radius: 6px; max-width: 720px;\">\n      <video src=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/mesh.mp4\" poster=\"https://shekerkamma.github.io/content-ideas/deepgrid-platform/media/mesh-poster.png\" controls preload=\"none\" playsinline style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 6px; background: #000; display: block;\"></video>\n      <div class=\"case-video-overlay\">\n        <div class=\"play-btn-circle\"><svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg></div>\n        <span class=\"play-btn-label\">Play 4-Petaflop 1024-Tile Mesh Architecture Video</span>\n      </div>\n      <span class=\"video-badge\"><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Video & Audio</span>\n    </div>\n    <figcaption><span class=\"figno\">Figure 11</span>Conceptual product. Silicon targets a <b>Q3 2029 tape-out</b>; the chassis ships 2030+. Peak figures are theoretical from the architecture spec and sustained figures are projected, pending simulator validation.<span class=\"figsrc\">Source &middot; Information Memorandum, p.17 &mdash; reproduced, not redrawn</span></figcaption></figure>\n    <div>\n      <p>Two reasons it belongs in an investor summary and not in the plan. It is <strong>funded from operating profit</strong>, not from this round &mdash; the model already carries a SoC4 5&nbsp;nm tapeout programme as an expense line growing to &#8377;169&nbsp;Cr by FY2032. And it is the clearest statement of what the company thinks it is: not an ADAS supplier that happens to own a die, but a design team that can aim the same architecture at a different market without starting over.</p>\n      <p>Price it as optionality. <strong>SoC2 is the business; this is the option the business buys you.</strong></p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"part\" id=\"usecases\">\n  <div class=\"part-head\"><span class=\"no\">Part III</span><h2>The use cases</h2><span class=\"cnt\">6 use cases &middot; 90-day sequence</span></div>\n<section>\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">Business use cases</p>\n  <h2>What a customer actually buys, and what Deepgrid is not selling them</h2>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Six use cases carry the commercial plan. Five are regulated functions a truck maker must source; the sixth is the only arena that can transact before qualified silicon exists.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"bound\">\n    <p class=\"lbl\">The bounding statement</p>\n    <p>Deepgrid sells a bounded camera-perception subsystem inside an accountable integrator&rsquo;s safety case. It does not own brake actuation, calibration, homologation or warranty &mdash; and no use case may be written as if it does.</p>\n  </div>\n  <p>That sentence is the most investor-relevant line in the whole file. It is what makes the Tier-1 sale possible, it caps the liability the company carries, and abandoning it is what would make the sale impossible.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"clock\">\n    <p class=\"clock-title\">Five mandated functions, and when the silicon arrives</p>\n    <div class=\"clock-grid\">\n      <div class=\"ck-axis\"><span>Function &middot; standard</span><span>1 Jan 2027</span><span>1 Oct 2027</span><span>1 Jan 2028</span><span>H1 2028</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ck-row\"><span class=\"fn\">Autonomous emergency braking<small>AIS-162 &middot; CMVR 96(12)</small></span><span class=\"ck-cell new\" data-l=\"New models\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell all\" data-l=\"All models\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"ck-row\"><span class=\"fn\">Driver drowsiness &amp; attention<small>AIS-184 &middot; CMVR 125Q(1)</small></span><span class=\"ck-cell\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell new\" data-l=\"New models\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell all\" data-l=\"All models\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"ck-row\"><span class=\"fn\">Blind-spot information<small>AIS-186 &middot; CMVR 125Q(2)</small></span><span class=\"ck-cell\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell new\" data-l=\"New models\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell all\" data-l=\"All models\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"ck-row\"><span class=\"fn\">Moving-off information<small>AIS-187 &middot; CMVR 125Q(3)</small></span><span class=\"ck-cell\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell new\" data-l=\"New models\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell all\" data-l=\"All models\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"ck-row\"><span class=\"fn\">Lane departure warning<small>AIS-188 &middot; CMVR 98(6)</small></span><span class=\"ck-cell\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell new\" data-l=\"New models\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell all\" data-l=\"All models\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"ck-row\"><span class=\"fn\">Deepgrid qualified ASIC silicon<small>everything before it is FPGA revenue</small></span><span class=\"ck-cell\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell\"></span><span class=\"ck-cell new\" data-l=\"Arrives\"></span></div>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"ck-note\">Four of the five functions bind on one clock, which is the design-in argument: a CV maker must source them together, so a supplier carrying several from one perception core is easier to nominate than four suppliers. <b>And the silicon arrives in the last column</b> &mdash; after every mandate date on the chart.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>The six below carry the commercial plan. Scan the matrix, then open whichever one you are pricing.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"tablewrap\">\n    <table>\n      <thead><tr><th></th><th>Function</th><th>Standard and rule</th><th>Binding dates</th><th>The gate that proves it</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr class=\"mx\"><td class=\"mxid\">UC-01</td><td>AEBS forward-path perception</td><td>AIS-162 / IS 11852:2019 &middot; CMVR 96(12)</td><td>1 Jan 2027 new models &middot; 1 Oct 2027 all models</td><td><span class=\"gatecell\">A braking Tier-1 accepts the interface, diagnostics, safety assumptions and validation plan in writing, with a recorded go/no-go.</span></td></tr>\n        <tr class=\"mx\"><td class=\"mxid\">UC-02</td><td>Nuisance-alert suppression</td><td>AIS-162 &sect;6.8 false-reaction test</td><td>Gates every AEBS approval from 1 Jan 2027</td><td><span class=\"gatecell\">One published equal-scope benchmark with scenario-stratified denominators and an independent agency&rsquo;s protocol.</span></td></tr>\n        <tr class=\"mx\"><td class=\"mxid\">UC-03</td><td>Blind-spot and moving-off information</td><td>AIS-186 &middot; AIS-187 &middot; CMVR 125Q(2)&ndash;(3)</td><td>1 Oct 2027 new models &middot; 1 Jan 2028 all models</td><td><span class=\"gatecell\">A characterised near-field result against both test geometries, with the false-information cases run, from an independent agency rather than a bench demo.</span></td></tr>\n        <tr class=\"mx\"><td class=\"mxid\">UC-04</td><td>Driver drowsiness and attention</td><td>AIS-184 (DDAWS) &middot; CMVR 125Q(1)</td><td>1 Oct 2027 new models &middot; 1 Jan 2028 all models</td><td><span class=\"gatecell\">A completed ten-participant day-and-night study with per-participant sensitivity and standard deviation, plus the assessable documentation package.</span></td></tr>\n        <tr class=\"mx\"><td class=\"mxid\">UC-05</td><td>Lane departure warning</td><td>AIS-188 (LDWS) &middot; CMVR 98(6)</td><td>1 Oct 2027 new models &middot; 1 Jan 2028 all models</td><td><span class=\"gatecell\">A measured corridor-estimation and alert result on unmarked and degraded Indian highway sections, reporting availability rate alongside false-alert rate.</span></td></tr>\n        <tr class=\"mx\"><td class=\"mxid\">UC-06</td><td>Government and PSU perception kit</td><td>PPP-MII Order 2017 (rev. 2020) &middot; GFR 153(iii)</td><td>Transactable now &mdash; does not wait for 2027</td><td><span class=\"gatecell\">A live GeM listing with documented local content at or above 50%, and one Class-I tender bid submitted with telemetry rights in the draft contract.</span></td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n\n  <details class=\"uc\">\n    <summary><span class=\"sid\">UC-01</span><span class=\"stitle\">Sell the braking Tier-1 the object list its safety case needs &mdash; never the brake decision</span><span class=\"smark\"></span></summary>\n    <div class=\"uc-top\"><span class=\"id\">UC-01</span><span>AEBS forward-path perception</span><span>AIS-162 / IS 11852:2019 &middot; CMVR 96(12)</span><span class=\"dates\">1 Jan 2027 new models &middot; 1 Oct 2027 all models</span></div>\n    <div class=\"uc-body\">\n      <div class=\"uc-cols\">\n        <div><h4>The challenge</h4><p>Rule 96(12) obliges AEBS plus Vehicle Stability Function on M2/M3/N2/N3. The system must warn at least 1.4&nbsp;s before it brakes and may not enter the emergency phase before TTC 3.0&nbsp;s. That budget is a perception problem; the braking is not.</p></div>\n        <div><h4>What Deepgrid supplies</h4><p>Detection, classification, tracking and per-target TTC on a documented interface, with confidence and sensor-health state. Actuation, calibration, homologation and warranty stay with the Tier-1.</p></div>\n      </div>\n      <ul class=\"uc-how\">\n        <li>Forward camera into the module: classify car, truck, bus, two- and three-wheeler, pedestrian and animal from 25&nbsp;km/h to max design speed, at every load state</li>\n        <li>Track each target, estimate range-rate, compute per-target TTC and in-path probability</li>\n        <li>Emit a ranked object list with per-object confidence and a degradation state on the interface the Tier-1 specifies</li>\n        <li>The Tier-1 arbitrates the warning cascade and owns the braking decision and its safety case</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"uc-stats\">\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">1.4 s / 0.8 s</span><span class=\"sl\">Warning-mode timing budget</span><span class=\"sn\">one haptic or acoustic mode, then two, before braking</span></div>\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">TTC &le; 3.0 s</span><span class=\"sl\">Earliest permitted braking</span><span class=\"sn\">the emergency phase may not start sooner</span></div>\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">4.23 lakh</span><span class=\"sl\">FY26 M&amp;HCV units</span><span class=\"sn\">the N2/N3/M3 envelope this rule binds</span></div>\n      </div>\n      <dl class=\"uc-foot\">\n        <div><dt>Who is in the room</dt><dd>Tier-1 ADAS system engineer &middot; functional-safety manager &middot; OEM chief engineer</dd></div>\n        <div><dt>Organisations</dt><dd>A braking Tier-1 &middot; CV OEM &middot; ARAI / ICAT</dd></div>\n        <div class=\"gate\"><dt>The gate that proves it</dt><dd>A braking Tier-1 accepts the interface, diagnostics, safety assumptions and validation plan in writing, with a recorded go/no-go.</dd></div>\n        <div class=\"risk\"><dt>The risk</dt><dd>No published ISO 26262 pathway. Until an assessor is engaged, the integrator is comparing a certified incumbent with an uncertified newcomer, and no perception result closes that gap.</dd></div>\n      </dl>\n    </div>\n  </details>\n  <details class=\"uc\">\n    <summary><span class=\"sid\">UC-02</span><span class=\"stitle\">The claim still available is the false alarm, not the detection</span><span class=\"smark\"></span></summary>\n    <div class=\"uc-top\"><span class=\"id\">UC-02</span><span>Nuisance-alert suppression</span><span>AIS-162 &sect;6.8 false-reaction test</span><span class=\"dates\">Gates every AEBS approval from 1 Jan 2027</span></div>\n    <div class=\"uc-body\">\n      <div class=\"uc-cols\">\n        <div><h4>The challenge</h4><p>Four rivals already claim India tuning. India-native is no longer a differentiator. What no competitor has published is a <em>measured nuisance rate</em> &mdash; and AIS-162 tests for exactly that.</p></div>\n        <div><h4>What Deepgrid supplies</h4><p>The denominator rather than the headline: a scenario-stratified false-positive rate per 1,000&nbsp;km against a named baseline, on the same silicon class, the same functions and the same test set.</p></div>\n      </div>\n      <ul class=\"uc-how\">\n        <li>Define the India nuisance set &mdash; overtaking two-wheelers, cut-in three-wheelers, cattle, roadside encroachment, unlit stationary trucks, wrong-way traffic, kerbside vending</li>\n        <li>Log every trigger <em>and every non-trigger</em> with scenario tags across three paid pilots, with telemetry rights secured in the contract</li>\n        <li>Score false positives per 1,000&nbsp;km and true-positive recall, stratified by scenario, lighting and monsoon</li>\n        <li>Publish at equal scope; withhold any comparison that silently changes what is being compared</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"uc-stats\">\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">50 &plusmn; 2 km/h</span><span class=\"sl\">False-reaction test speed</span><span class=\"sn\">the pass the module must survive in silence</span></div>\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">&ge; 60 m</span><span class=\"sl\">Between two stationary vehicles</span><span class=\"sn\">no warning, no emergency braking, or it fails</span></div>\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">0</span><span class=\"sl\">Published India nuisance rates</span><span class=\"sn\">by any competitor in the retrieved corpus</span></div>\n      </div>\n      <dl class=\"uc-foot\">\n        <div><dt>Who is in the room</dt><dd>Head of Validation &middot; Tier-1 evaluation engineer &middot; fleet safety manager</dd></div>\n        <div><dt>Organisations</dt><dd>ARAI or ICAT &middot; three paid pilot fleets &middot; the Tier-1 running the evaluation</dd></div>\n        <div class=\"gate\"><dt>The gate that proves it</dt><dd>One published equal-scope benchmark with scenario-stratified denominators and an independent agency&rsquo;s protocol.</dd></div>\n        <div class=\"risk\"><dt>The risk</dt><dd>A nuisance rate without a denominator is marketing. If scenario mix, kilometres and baseline are not fixed in advance, the result will be discounted to zero in a Tier-1 review.</dd></div>\n      </dl>\n    </div>\n  </details>\n  <details class=\"uc\">\n    <summary><span class=\"sid\">UC-03</span><span class=\"stitle\">Two-thirds of India&rsquo;s road deaths are the road users these two standards were written for</span><span class=\"smark\"></span></summary>\n    <div class=\"uc-top\"><span class=\"id\">UC-03</span><span>Blind-spot and moving-off information</span><span>AIS-186 &middot; AIS-187 &middot; CMVR 125Q(2)&ndash;(3)</span><span class=\"dates\">1 Oct 2027 new models &middot; 1 Jan 2028 all models</span></div>\n    <div class=\"uc-body\">\n      <div class=\"uc-cols\">\n        <div><h4>The challenge</h4><p>Two-wheeler riders were 46.2% of India&rsquo;s 1,77,175 road deaths in 2024 and pedestrians 20.6%. AIS-186 demands an information signal 15&nbsp;m before the expected collision point and forbids manual deactivation.</p></div>\n        <div><h4>What Deepgrid supplies</h4><p>One India-trained perception core with two output contracts &mdash; near-field side and near-field front. Same silicon, same corpus, different detection geometry and signal timing.</p></div>\n      </div>\n      <ul class=\"uc-how\">\n        <li>Side and front near-field cameras into the module; classify pedestrian, adult cyclist and child cyclist</li>\n        <li>Project turn geometry including the counter-turn; raise the signal at least 15&nbsp;m before the collision point and hold it through the manoeuvre</li>\n        <li>Detect VRUs crossing at 3&ndash;5&nbsp;km/h and cyclists parallel at 0&ndash;10&nbsp;km/h inside the 3.7&nbsp;m plane; hold through standstill until 15&nbsp;m past the stopping point</li>\n        <li>Pass the false-information tests, including the traffic-sign case</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"uc-stats\">\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">67%</span><span class=\"sl\">Of 2024 road deaths</span><span class=\"sn\">pedestrians and two-wheeler riders &mdash; 1.28 lakh people</span></div>\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">15 m</span><span class=\"sl\">Signal lead before collision point</span><span class=\"sn\">and it may not be switched off</span></div>\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">3.7 m</span><span class=\"sl\">Forward plane</span><span class=\"sn\">the close-proximity blind spot in front of the cab</span></div>\n      </div>\n      <dl class=\"uc-foot\">\n        <div><dt>Who is in the room</dt><dd>OEM cab and body engineer &middot; Tier-1 HMI owner &middot; fleet safety officer &middot; driver</dd></div>\n        <div><dt>Organisations</dt><dd>CV OEM &middot; bus body builder &middot; state transport undertaking &middot; ARAI / ICAT</dd></div>\n        <div class=\"gate\"><dt>The gate that proves it</dt><dd>A characterised near-field result against both test geometries, with the false-information cases run, from an independent agency rather than a bench demo.</dd></div>\n        <div class=\"risk\"><dt>The risk</dt><dd>The signal cannot be switched off, so a high nuisance rate is permanently in the driver&rsquo;s peripheral vision. UC-02 is a prerequisite, not a parallel track.</dd></div>\n      </dl>\n    </div>\n  </details>\n  <details class=\"uc\">\n    <summary><span class=\"sid\">UC-04</span><span class=\"stitle\">The only mandated function whose approval evidence is a human-subject study, not a track run</span><span class=\"smark\"></span></summary>\n    <div class=\"uc-top\"><span class=\"id\">UC-04</span><span>Driver drowsiness and attention</span><span>AIS-184 (DDAWS) &middot; CMVR 125Q(1)</span><span class=\"dates\">1 Oct 2027 new models &middot; 1 Jan 2028 all models</span></div>\n    <div class=\"uc-body\">\n      <div class=\"uc-cols\">\n        <div><h4>The challenge</h4><p>Approval is not a track test. The manufacturer must run at least ten participants, none from the development team, in day and night, generating ten or more true-positive or false-negative events, and report per-participant sensitivity.</p></div>\n        <div><h4>What Deepgrid supplies</h4><p>An in-cab drowsiness pipeline delivered <em>together with the study that makes it approvable</em>. The differentiator is not the model &mdash; it is handing the integrator a completed documentation package instead of a demonstration.</p></div>\n      </div>\n      <ul class=\"uc-how\">\n        <li>In-cab infrared camera into the module: eyelid closure, gaze, head pose and PERCLOS-class metrics, working at night</li>\n        <li>Fuse with vehicle signals &mdash; reduced steering micro-corrections paired with larger, faster ones, and lateral lane-position variability</li>\n        <li>Warn above KSS level 8; escalate visual then acoustic per the HMI specification</li>\n        <li>Run the ten-participant study and deliver metrics, thresholds, activation speed, weather limits and the statistical analysis</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"uc-stats\">\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">KSS &gt; 8</span><span class=\"sl\">Warning threshold</span><span class=\"sn\">the drowsiness level at which an alert is required</span></div>\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">10</span><span class=\"sl\">Minimum participants</span><span class=\"sn\">none of whom may have developed the system</span></div>\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">Before silicon</span><span class=\"sl\">Can start now</span><span class=\"sn\">the bottleneck is a study, not a tapeout</span></div>\n      </div>\n      <dl class=\"uc-foot\">\n        <div><dt>Who is in the room</dt><dd>Fleet safety manager &middot; driver &middot; OEM homologation engineer &middot; testing-agency assessor</dd></div>\n        <div><dt>Organisations</dt><dd>CV OEM &middot; ARAI or ICAT &middot; fleet operator &middot; the ten-participant cohort</dd></div>\n        <div class=\"gate\"><dt>The gate that proves it</dt><dd>A completed ten-participant day-and-night study with per-participant sensitivity and standard deviation, plus the assessable documentation package.</dd></div>\n        <div class=\"risk\"><dt>The risk</dt><dd>Intra-city, school and double-decker buses are outside scope unless the maker opts in. Sizing against all M2/M3 volume overstates this, and an urban-bus fleet is the wrong first pilot.</dd></div>\n      </dl>\n    </div>\n  </details>\n  <details class=\"uc\">\n    <summary><span class=\"sid\">UC-05</span><span class=\"stitle\">The function India&rsquo;s road surface makes hardest and the mandate makes unavoidable</span><span class=\"smark\"></span></summary>\n    <div class=\"uc-top\"><span class=\"id\">UC-05</span><span>Lane departure warning</span><span>AIS-188 (LDWS) &middot; CMVR 98(6)</span><span class=\"dates\">1 Oct 2027 new models &middot; 1 Jan 2028 all models</span></div>\n    <div class=\"uc-body\">\n      <div class=\"uc-cols\">\n        <div><h4>The challenge</h4><p>58.6% of 2024 road deaths were on national and state highways &mdash; about 5% of the network &mdash; and 67.6% of accidents happened on straight roads, precisely where LDWS applies. Yet markings on those corridors are worn, inconsistent or absent.</p></div>\n        <div><h4>What Deepgrid supplies</h4><p>Lane estimation that does not depend on a painted line: road edge, kerb, median, worn marking and vehicle-flow cues fused into a drivable-corridor estimate, with thresholds that move with traffic density and speed.</p></div>\n      </div>\n      <ul class=\"uc-how\">\n        <li>Segment lane marking, road edge, kerb and median, and estimate marking quality</li>\n        <li>Estimate the drivable corridor and lateral position when no marking is visible</li>\n        <li>Modulate the departure threshold by traffic density and speed; suppress during indicated manoeuvres</li>\n        <li>Emit the departure event with confidence, plus an explicit temporarily-unavailable state</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"uc-stats\">\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">58.6%</span><span class=\"sl\">Of 2024 road deaths</span><span class=\"sn\">on NH and SH &mdash; about 5% of the road network</span></div>\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">67.6%</span><span class=\"sl\">Of accidents on straight roads</span><span class=\"sn\">the road feature where LDWS is the applicable function</span></div>\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">Same sensor</span><span class=\"sl\">As UC-01</span><span class=\"sn\">the cheapest second function to offer a Tier-1 already evaluating</span></div>\n      </div>\n      <dl class=\"uc-foot\">\n        <div><dt>Who is in the room</dt><dd>OEM chassis and ADAS engineer &middot; Tier-1 integrator &middot; long-haul driver</dd></div>\n        <div><dt>Organisations</dt><dd>CV OEM &middot; Tier-1 &middot; highway fleet operators &middot; ARAI / ICAT</dd></div>\n        <div class=\"gate\"><dt>The gate that proves it</dt><dd>A measured corridor-estimation and alert result on unmarked and degraded Indian highway sections, reporting availability rate alongside false-alert rate.</dd></div>\n        <div class=\"risk\"><dt>The risk</dt><dd>Declaring the function unavailable too readily is the easy way to pass a nuisance target and the fast way to fail type approval. Both numbers must be reported together or neither means anything.</dd></div>\n      </dl>\n    </div>\n  </details>\n  <details class=\"uc\">\n    <summary><span class=\"sid\">UC-06</span><span class=\"stitle\">The only arena that can transact before qualified silicon exists</span><span class=\"smark\"></span></summary>\n    <div class=\"uc-top\"><span class=\"id\">UC-06</span><span>Government and PSU perception kit</span><span>PPP-MII Order 2017 (rev. 2020) &middot; GFR 153(iii)</span><span class=\"dates\">Transactable now &mdash; does not wait for 2027</span></div>\n    <div class=\"uc-body\">\n      <div class=\"uc-cols\">\n        <div><h4>The challenge</h4><p>The shipping product is an FPGA module. Qualified volume silicon lands H1 2028 &mdash; <em>after</em> the mandate&rsquo;s all-models date &mdash; and OEM design-in runs 18 to 30 months. Every rupee before H1 2028 has to come from the FPGA module.</p></div>\n        <div><h4>What Deepgrid supplies</h4><p>The module packaged as a GeM-listed Class-I local-content perception kit for state transport undertakings and PSU fleets, where the gate is <em>eligibility</em> rather than certification.</p></div>\n      </div>\n      <ul class=\"uc-how\">\n        <li>Compute and document local content at or above 50%, self-certified with the locations of value addition</li>\n        <li>List on GeM with country of origin and local-content percentage, qualifying for the Make in India filter</li>\n        <li>Bid into STU, PSU and municipal tenders reserved for or preference-weighted toward Class-I suppliers</li>\n        <li>Instrument every delivered unit and secure telemetry rights in the supply contract &mdash; these units are the evidence engine for UC-02</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"uc-stats\">\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">&ge; 50%</span><span class=\"sl\">Local content</span><span class=\"sn\">the threshold that makes Deepgrid a Class-I local supplier</span></div>\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">20%</span><span class=\"sl\">Margin of purchase preference</span><span class=\"sn\">over a non-Class-I lowest bid, with a right to match</span></div>\n        <div><span class=\"sv\">H1 2028</span><span class=\"sl\">Qualified ASIC arrives</span><span class=\"sn\">everything before it is FPGA-module revenue</span></div>\n      </div>\n      <dl class=\"uc-foot\">\n        <div><dt>Who is in the room</dt><dd>STU procurement officer &middot; depot engineer &middot; Deepgrid BD &middot; Head of Validation</dd></div>\n        <div><dt>Organisations</dt><dd>State transport undertakings &middot; PSU and municipal fleets &middot; defence procurement &middot; GeM</dd></div>\n        <div class=\"gate\"><dt>The gate that proves it</dt><dd>A live GeM listing with documented local content at or above 50%, and one Class-I tender bid submitted with telemetry rights in the draft contract.</dd></div>\n        <div class=\"risk\"><dt>The risk</dt><dd>An incumbent already draws about 30% of revenue from government tenders and can underbid on empanelment. Class-I status is winnable but slowly, and a nodal ministry may prescribe local content above 50%.</dd></div>\n      </dl>\n    </div>\n  </details>\n</section><section>\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">Ninety days</p>\n  <h2>The sequence, and what capital is explicitly not for</h2>\n  <ol class=\"seq\">\n    <li><span class=\"win\">Now &ndash; 30 days</span><span class=\"act\">GeM listing prepared &middot; nuisance taxonomy and protocol drafted with ARAI or ICAT &middot; ISO 26262 assessor engaged as a procurement action</span><span class=\"own\">CEO &middot; CTO</span></li>\n    <li><span class=\"win\">30 &ndash; 60 days</span><span class=\"act\">Technical exchange opened with a braking Tier-1 &middot; three paid pilots contracted with telemetry rights &middot; drowsiness study cohort assembled</span><span class=\"own\">CEO &middot; Validation</span></li>\n    <li><span class=\"win\">60 &ndash; 90 days</span><span class=\"act\">First stratified nuisance result published &middot; first Class-I bid submitted &middot; written go/no-go recorded from the Tier-1 exchange</span><span class=\"own\">Validation &middot; BD</span></li>\n  </ol>\n  <div class=\"flag\"><h3>Do not fund</h3>\n  <p>A full-stack braking safety case &middot; broad OEM customisation &middot; a radar programme of any kind &middot; any performance marketing not backed by a measured result. Release capital only when partner access, field telemetry and a primary qualification artifact clear together.</p></div>\n</section>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"part\" id=\"choice\">\n  <div class=\"part-head\"><span class=\"no\">Part IV</span><h2>The strategic choice and its economics</h2><span class=\"cnt\">5 options &middot; 1 recommendation &middot; 1 threshold</span></div>\n<section>\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">The decision</p>\n  <h2>The company has a mandate it cannot yet serve and a chip that arrives after it</h2>\n\n  <div class=\"decision\">\n    <p class=\"lbl\">The strategic decision</p>\n    <p>How does Deepgrid bridge the ~24 months between the mandate wave and its own qualified silicon &mdash; and which lane compounds into the &#8377;1,128&nbsp;Cr plan rather than merely surviving the gap?</p>\n    <p>Four constraints bound every answer. Cash is <strong>&#8377;2.5 lakh</strong>, so the first lane must produce revenue in months, not years. The <strong>15 provisional patents carry a March 2027 conversion deadline</strong> that no use-of-funds line pays for. <strong>No ISO 26262 assessor is engaged</strong>, which gates the highest-value lane entirely. And the post-raise team is ten engineers with a CTO who is not yet full-time &mdash; enough to run two lanes properly, not five.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>The plan implies a path without ever arguing for it. That is the gap this section closes: five lanes were available, and the reason to pick one is not that it is the only one, but that it is the only one whose output is the next lane's input.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"opts\">\n    <div class=\"opt pick\">\n      <span class=\"oid\">Option A<small>Recommended<br>Lead lane</small></span>\n      <div>\n        <h3>Government and PSU wedge &mdash; sell the FPGA module where the gate is eligibility</h3>\n        <p class=\"od\">List the module on GeM as a Class-I local-content perception kit and bid into state transport undertaking, PSU and municipal tenders. At &ge;50% local content the company earns a 20% margin of purchase preference and a right to match. This is the only arena where the gate is <em>eligibility</em>, which Deepgrid can satisfy today, rather than certification, which it cannot.</p>\n        <dl>\n          <div class=\"up\"><dt>Upside</dt><dd>Revenue in months on hardware that already exists &mdash; and every delivered unit is an instrumented vehicle.</dd></div>\n          <div><dt>Trade-off</dt><dd>Warning-only retrofit, price-competitive, and an incumbent already draws ~30% of its revenue from these tenders.</dd></div>\n          <div class=\"mbt\"><dt>What must be true</dt><dd>Local content on the real bill of materials clears 50%, and telemetry rights survive a public-procurement contract.</dd></div>\n        </dl>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"opt pick\">\n      <span class=\"oid\">Option B<small>Recommended<br>Run in parallel</small></span>\n      <div>\n        <h3>Tier-1 attach &mdash; sell bounded perception into someone else&rsquo;s safety case</h3>\n        <p class=\"od\">Supply detection, classification, tracking and per-target time-to-collision on a documented interface to a braking Tier-1 already nominated on an OEM programme. Actuation, calibration, homologation and warranty stay with the Tier-1 &mdash; the division that makes the sale possible at all.</p>\n        <dl>\n          <div class=\"up\"><dt>Upside</dt><dd>The highest terminal value in the portfolio. This is the &#8377;450&nbsp;Cr truck line and the platform prize behind it.</dd></div>\n          <div><dt>Trade-off</dt><dd>Design-in runs 18&ndash;30 months, so the January 2027 date is already unwinnable and first revenue is FY2029.</dd></div>\n          <div class=\"mbt\"><dt>What must be true</dt><dd>An ISO 26262 assessor is engaged and funded &mdash; it appears in no use-of-funds line &mdash; and one Tier-1 records a written go.</dd></div>\n        </dl>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"opt\">\n      <span class=\"oid\">Option C<small>Ring-fence,<br>do not lead</small></span>\n      <div>\n        <h3>Defence-first &mdash; make the secure-compute chiplet the revenue engine</h3>\n        <p class=\"od\">Lead with D100 and the D-HUMR platform through iDEX, DRDO and the MCEME pipeline, where indigenous-procurement rules exclude every import-dependent competitor by specification rather than by price.</p>\n        <dl>\n          <div class=\"up\"><dt>Upside</dt><dd>Near-zero competition, a procurement route independent of the automotive mandate, and a clean carve-out exit vector.</dd></div>\n          <div><dt>Trade-off</dt><dd>&#8377;30&nbsp;Cr of the plan &mdash; 2.7%. Defence telemetry produces nothing that transfers to road perception.</dd></div>\n          <div class=\"mbt\"><dt>What must be true</dt><dd>The IP position is resolved. Delivered revenue is &#8377;23.01L, it sits in a different legal entity, and the IP is MCEME-owned.</dd></div>\n        </dl>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"opt\">\n      <span class=\"oid\">Option D<small>Correctly deferred<br>to FY2029</small></span>\n      <div>\n        <h3>Licence-first &mdash; sell the core instead of the product</h3>\n        <p class=\"od\">Pull T100 IP licensing forward from FY2029: no bill of materials, no installer, no warranty logistics, 90%+ margin on every rupee.</p>\n        <dl>\n          <div class=\"up\"><dt>Upside</dt><dd>The cleanest economics in the plan and the only line that needs no operational capacity whatsoever.</dd></div>\n          <div><dt>Trade-off</dt><dd>Nobody licences an unproven core, and licensing the core undercuts the systems business that is 88% of revenue.</dd></div>\n          <div class=\"mbt\"><dt>What must be true</dt><dd>Silicon has a track record first &mdash; which is precisely why the model already places this line in FY2029.</dd></div>\n        </dl>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"opt\">\n      <span class=\"oid\">Option E<small>Reject as a<br>standalone</small></span>\n      <div>\n        <h3>Silicon sprint &mdash; spend the round on the tapeout and treat interim revenue as noise</h3>\n        <p class=\"od\">Compress everything into reaching qualified silicon, accept that FY2027&ndash;28 revenue is immaterial, and run the company as a single-milestone entity until H1 2028.</p>\n        <dl>\n          <div class=\"up\"><dt>Upside</dt><dd>Fastest route to the asset that actually creates enterprise value, and the simplest story to tell.</dd></div>\n          <div><dt>Trade-off</dt><dd>Money does not compress a fab schedule much, and a slip has no revenue underneath it to absorb the delay.</dd></div>\n          <div class=\"mbt\"><dt>What must be true</dt><dd>&#8377;45&nbsp;Cr covers 24 months with no parallel revenue &mdash; and this is what the round already is if no lane is chosen deliberately.</dd></div>\n        </dl>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"evalwrap\">\n    <table class=\"eval\">\n      <thead><tr><th>Criterion &mdash; drawn from this decision, not a generic scorecard</th><th class=\"c\">A &middot; Gov</th><th class=\"c\">B &middot; Tier-1</th><th class=\"c\">C &middot; Defence</th><th class=\"c\">D &middot; Licence</th><th class=\"c\">E &middot; Silicon</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td>Cash to first rupee<small>against a &#8377;2.5 lakh balance</small></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt4\">Months</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt1\">FY2029</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt4\">Months</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt1\">FY2029</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt1\">H1 2028</span></td></tr>\n        <tr><td>What actually gates it<small>the blocker, not the effort</small></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt4\">Eligibility</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt1\">Cert + trust</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt3\">Procurement</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt2\">Track record</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt2\">Fab schedule</span></td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Works on the FPGA module<small>survives the pre-silicon window</small></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt4\">Yes</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt3\">Partly</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt4\">Yes</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt1\">No</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt1\">N/A</span></td></tr>\n        <tr class=\"pickcol\"><td>Builds the evidence engine<small>scenario-tagged nuisance data &mdash; the one open contest</small></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt4\">Produces it</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt3\">Consumes it</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt2\">No transfer</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt2\">None</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt2\">None</span></td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Terminal value<small>does it reach the plan or cap out</small></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt2\">Capped</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt4\">Highest</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt2\">&#8377;30 Cr</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt3\">&#8377;50 Cr</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt4\">Full plan</span></td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Team load<small>ten engineers, part-time CTO</small></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt4\">Low</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt2\">High</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt3\">2 FTE</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt4\">Low</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt2\">All of it</span></td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Concentration effect<small>on the 64% two-product problem</small></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt3\">Reduces</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt1\">Deepens</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt4\">Diversifies</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt3\">Diversifies</span></td><td class=\"c\"><span class=\"rt1\">Deepens</span></td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"recc\">\n    <div class=\"recc-in\">\n      <p class=\"lbl\">Recommendation</p>\n      <h3>Run A for B, not A then B</h3>\n      <p><strong>Lead with the government wedge and open the Tier-1 exchange in the same month.</strong> The temptation is to read Option A as a way to survive until the real business starts. That is the wrong reading, and it costs the company its only open differentiator.</p>\n      <p>The dossier is explicit that India-native perception is <em>no longer</em> a differentiator &mdash; four rivals already claim it. The one contest whose result is not yet written is the <strong>measured nuisance rate</strong>, because no competitor has published one. Producing that number needs instrumented vehicles running Indian roads with scenario tags applied at capture and telemetry rights secured in the contract. <strong>Option A is the only lane that generates exactly that</strong> &mdash; and the number it generates is the single strongest thing Deepgrid can put in front of the Tier-1 in Option B.</p>\n      <p>So the sequencing is not defensive. Government units are the sensor network that produces the evidence that wins the design-in. Sequence them A-then-B and the data arrives too late to matter; run A <em>for</em> B and the pre-silicon window becomes the thing that makes the post-silicon business winnable.</p>\n      <div class=\"chain\">\n        <span class=\"on\">A &middot; GeM units shipping</span><b>&rarr;</b><span class=\"on\">Telemetry &amp; scenario tags</span><b>&rarr;</b><span class=\"on\">Published nuisance rate</span><b>&rarr;</b><span class=\"on\">Tier-1 go/no-go</span><b>&rarr;</b><span>Design-in on silicon</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <p><strong>Ring-fence C, defer D, reject E as a standalone.</strong> Defence stays a separate two-engineer lane with its own procurement route and its own exit vector &mdash; valuable precisely because it is uncorrelated with the mandate, and not a candidate to lead because its telemetry transfers nothing. Licensing stays where the model already puts it. And Option E is what this round becomes by default if no lane is chosen deliberately, which is the argument for choosing.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\" style=\"margin-top:34px\">Before committing</p>\n  <h2>Four questions that would change this recommendation</h2>\n  <p>Each of these is an assumption the recommendation rests on, and none of them is validated in any document reviewed. Two carry a dated cash call that appears in no use-of-funds line.</p>\n  <ol class=\"mbt-list\">\n    <li><span class=\"n\">01</span><span class=\"q\"><b>Does the real bill of materials clear 50% local content?</b> Class-I status is the entire basis of Option A, and no document reviewed computes it. Compute it on the actual BOM with imported content valued in, before the GeM listing is drafted.</span><span class=\"st\">Unvalidated</span></li>\n    <li><span class=\"n\">02</span><span class=\"q\"><b>Do telemetry rights survive a public-procurement contract?</b> The evidence engine only exists if the data can be retained. Pull one state transport undertaking&rsquo;s standard contract and check admissibility before the first bid, not after the first award.</span><span class=\"st\">Unvalidated</span></li>\n    <li><span class=\"n\">03</span><span class=\"q\"><b>What does an ISO 26262 assessor cost, and where is it funded from?</b> It gates Option B entirely, the use-of-funds carries AIS-162/188 certification only, and the company&rsquo;s own 30-day plan lists engaging one as a procurement action.</span><span class=\"st\">Unfunded</span></li>\n    <li><span class=\"n\">04</span><span class=\"q\"><b>Who pays to convert 15 provisional patents by March 2027?</b> Provisionals must become complete specifications within twelve months of the March 2026 priority date. That is a hard, dated cash call on the IP the whole thesis rests on, and it appears in no allocation line.</span><span class=\"st\">Unfunded &middot; dated</span></li>\n  </ol>\n</section>\n\n<section>\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">The business case</p>\n  <h2>The round clears self-funding by &#8377;10.1 crore, and both missing lines land inside it</h2>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Pricing the recommended path against the model&rsquo;s own cash schedule produces one number that decides the round, and it is not the terminal year.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"runway\">\n    <p class=\"rw-title\">Closing cash balance &#8377; Cr &middot; base case, from the model&rsquo;s own runway schedule</p>\n    <div class=\"rw-plot\">\n      <div class=\"rw-band\"></div><span class=\"rw-lbl\">&#8595; The entire margin of safety &mdash; &#8377;10.1 Cr</span>\n      <div class=\"rw-col open\"><span class=\"rw-val\">45.03</span><span class=\"rw-bar\" style=\"height:90%\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"rw-col\"><span class=\"rw-val\">25.28</span><span class=\"rw-bar\" style=\"height:50.6%\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"rw-col\"><span class=\"rw-val\">11.35</span><span class=\"rw-bar\" style=\"height:22.7%\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"rw-col trough\"><span class=\"rw-val\">10.10</span><span class=\"rw-bar\" style=\"height:20.2%\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"rw-col\"><span class=\"rw-val\">32.53</span><span class=\"rw-bar\" style=\"height:65.1%\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"rw-col clip\"><span class=\"rw-val\">111.16</span><span class=\"rw-bar\" style=\"height:100%\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"rw-col clip\"><span class=\"rw-val\">313.58</span><span class=\"rw-bar\" style=\"height:100%\"></span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"rw-x\"><span>Opening</span><span>FY2027</span><span>FY2028</span><span>FY2029</span><span>FY2030</span><span>FY2031 &uarr;</span><span>FY2032 &uarr;</span></div>\n    <p class=\"rw-note\">Axis capped at &#8377;50&nbsp;Cr; the last two columns are clipped. The model&rsquo;s verdict on this schedule is &ldquo;funded to self-sustaining&rdquo;, and on its own terms that is correct. <b>But the trough is &#8377;10.098&nbsp;Cr on a &#8377;45&nbsp;Cr round &mdash; a 22% margin of safety, with no contingency line anywhere in the use of funds.</b> The undrawn &#8377;10&nbsp;Cr CGTMSE facility is not in this schedule, and is almost exactly the size of the trough.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"thresh\">\n    <p class=\"lbl\">The decision threshold</p>\n    <p>The round works if the two unfunded lines come in under roughly <strong>&#8377;10 crore combined</strong> and the CGTMSE facility is genuinely available to draw. Above that, this is a short round wearing a full one.</p>\n    <p>Both lines land in FY2027&ndash;28, the same window as the &#8377;18&nbsp;Cr and &#8377;10&nbsp;Cr tapeout draws &mdash; patent conversion because the March 2027 deadline is fixed, and the functional-safety assessor because the Tier-1 exchange opens in month one. Neither can be deferred past the trough. Do not accept a term sheet before both are quoted.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"tablewrap\">\n    <table class=\"econ\">\n      <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th class=\"n\">Downside &middot; 0.3&times;</th><th class=\"n base\">Base</th><th class=\"n\">Upside &middot; 1.2&times;</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td>FY2032 revenue &#8377; Cr</td><td class=\"n\">338.5</td><td class=\"n base\">1,128.45</td><td class=\"n\">1,354.1</td><td>Model, scenario multiplier</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>FY2032 EBITDA &#8377; Cr</td><td class=\"n\">not published</td><td class=\"n base\">387.88</td><td class=\"n\">not published</td><td>Model, base only</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>FY2032 gross margin</td><td class=\"n\">not published</td><td class=\"n base\">87.4%</td><td class=\"n\">not published</td><td>Model, base only</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>First EBITDA-positive year</td><td class=\"n\">not published</td><td class=\"n base\">FY2028</td><td class=\"n\">not published</td><td>Model, base only</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><strong>Minimum cash balance &#8377; Cr</strong></td><td class=\"n\">not published</td><td class=\"n base\"><strong>10.10</strong></td><td class=\"n\">not published</td><td>Model, base only</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Year of the trough</td><td class=\"n\">not published</td><td class=\"n base\">FY2029</td><td class=\"n\">not published</td><td>Model, base only</td></tr>\n        <tr class=\"total\"><td>Contingency line</td><td class=\"n\">&mdash;</td><td class=\"n base\">none</td><td class=\"n\">&mdash;</td><td>Use of funds &mdash; four lines, no reserve</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n  <p>The workbook switches scenarios live, so the cash schedule does recompute &mdash; but only the base case is published. <strong>A downside cash trough is a diligence request, not a number anyone has seen.</strong> Ask for it before the term sheet: it is one cell.</p>\n\n  <h2 style=\"margin-top:44px\">Four load-bearing assumptions, and how hard each one leans</h2>\n  <div class=\"tablewrap\">\n    <table>\n      <thead><tr><th>Driver</th><th>The assumption</th><th>Evidence behind it</th><th>Confidence</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td>FY2027 revenue mix</td><td>&#8377;1.20&nbsp;Cr of the &#8377;1.70&nbsp;Cr first year &mdash; <strong>71%</strong> &mdash; comes from the defence humanoid line</td><td>Substantiated delivered revenue is <strong>&#8377;23.01L</strong>. The assumption is 5.2&times; that, on the single largest line of the first year.</td><td><span class=\"conf lo\">Weak</span></td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Opex behaviour in a miss</td><td>Operating expense is modelled as a percentage of revenue, so a revenue shortfall shrinks cost with it</td><td>Real payroll, R&amp;D and the &#8377;30&nbsp;Cr tapeout do not shrink because sales miss. This is what makes &ldquo;a 70% miss still self-funds&rdquo; true in the model and untested in reality.</td><td><span class=\"conf lo\">Weak</span></td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Unit capture</td><td>AD2 takes 1.8% of a 1.0M mandated pool; no line exceeds 2% of its own market</td><td>Pool sized from MoRTH and third-party sources; the capture rates are management assumptions. Every pool is global while the serviceable market is the India slice.</td><td><span class=\"conf md\">Moderate</span></td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Die cost at volume</td><td>$3.88 per die, breaking even on NRE at 174,908 chips against ~217,000 planned through FY2032</td><td>Foundry quotation with 94.5% mature-node yield and a 300&nbsp;mm wafer at a volume-committed price. <strong>A 20% volume miss pushes breakeven past the plan&rsquo;s final year.</strong></td><td><span class=\"conf hi\">Strong</span></td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n  <p>Prices are held flat across all six years, so there is no price lever hidden in the forecast &mdash; every rupee of growth is volume. That is a modelling choice worth crediting: it removes the easiest place to bury an assumption, and it means a 10% ASP erosion on the two concentrated lines takes roughly <span class=\"num\">&#8377;72 Cr</span> straight off FY2032 with nothing to offset it.</p>\n\n  <h2 style=\"margin-top:44px\">The scenario set tests the wrong variable</h2>\n  <p>The model runs Bull, Bear and Downside by scaling revenue &mdash; 1.2&times;, 0.75&times;, 0.3&times; &mdash; and adjusting opex as a percentage of it. Every one of those is a <em>demand</em> test. But demand is the most defensible thing in this plan: it is legislated, the pools are sourced, and no line assumes more than 2% capture.</p>\n  <p><strong>The variable that actually breaks this company is schedule.</strong> A tapeout slip pushes qualified silicon past H1 2028 into a window where the mandate has already closed, the FPGA lane is competing on price, and the fixed cost block &mdash; payroll, R&amp;D, the remaining mask commitment &mdash; keeps running at full rate because none of it is a function of revenue. That case is not modelled anywhere.</p>\n  <p>Ask for two more scenarios before the term sheet: <strong>a six-month silicon slip</strong>, and <strong>a fixed-cost floor</strong> in which opex holds at plan while revenue misses. Those are the two that decide whether &#8377;45&nbsp;Cr is the right number.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"verdictbox\">\n    <div class=\"verdictbox-in\">\n      <p class=\"lbl\">Recommendation</p>\n      <h3>Proceed &mdash; and re-cut the use of funds before the term sheet, not after</h3>\n      <p>The case holds. The asset is real, the demand is legislated, the unit economics are the strongest part of the plan, and the staged tapeout already gives an investor four places to stop. Nothing found here argues against funding it.</p>\n      <p>What it argues against is funding it <em>on the current allocation</em>. Four lines and no reserve, with a &#8377;10.1&nbsp;Cr trough and two dated obligations that appear nowhere, is a use of funds that has not been asked the questions above. All four fixes are arithmetic, none of them changes the business, and all four are cheaper to make now than to discover in FY2029.</p>\n      <ol class=\"actions\">\n        <li><span class=\"n\">01</span><span class=\"a\"><b>Quote and insert the two missing lines.</b> Patent conversion by March 2027 and a functional-safety assessor. If they clear &#8377;10&nbsp;Cr combined, the round is short and should be sized up rather than squeezed.</span><span class=\"w\">Before term sheet</span></li>\n        <li><span class=\"n\">02</span><span class=\"a\"><b>Reclassify the CGTMSE facility as declared contingency.</b> It is not in the cash schedule and it is almost exactly the size of the trough. Calling it working capital hides the only reserve the plan has.</span><span class=\"w\">Before term sheet</span></li>\n        <li><span class=\"n\">03</span><span class=\"a\"><b>Re-forecast FY2027 without the &#8377;1.2 Cr defence assumption.</b> Rebuild the first year from the delivered &#8377;23.01L plus the government lane, and show what the FPGA window actually earns.</span><span class=\"w\">Before term sheet</span></li>\n        <li><span class=\"n\">04</span><span class=\"a\"><b>Publish a schedule-slip and a fixed-cost-floor scenario.</b> The existing downside tests demand, which is the defensible half. Test the half that is not.</span><span class=\"w\">Before term sheet</span></li>\n      </ol>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>One structural note that no fix reaches: <strong>the recommended path has no revenue line in the model.</strong> The government and PSU lane is the first lane the strategy calls for and the only one transactable today, and it appears nowhere in the fifteen-line build &mdash; folded, at best, into the mirror and truck-kit lines it is meant to precede. A plan whose first eighteen months are carried by a channel the forecast does not name is a plan that cannot be tracked against itself. Give it a line.</p>\n</section>\n\n</div>\n<div class=\"part\" id=\"numbers\">\n  <div class=\"part-head\"><span class=\"no\">Part V</span><h2>The numbers and the risk</h2><span class=\"cnt\">3 sections &middot; 10 flags</span></div>\n<section>\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">The plan</p>\n  <h2>The ramp is gated by the chip &mdash; which is what the round funds</h2>\n  <p>Six products earn revenue in FY2027, nine more in FY2028, and the licence line starts later still. FY2027 is <strong>&#8377;1.7 Cr across six products on FPGA hardware</strong> &mdash; deliberately small, and honest about it. ASIC revenue starts FY2028 at the earliest.</p>\n  <div class=\"ramp\">\n    <p class=\"ramp-title\">Revenue &#8377; Cr &middot; bottom-up units &times; ASP, no target plug</p>\n    <div class=\"ramp-rows\">\n      <div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"yr\">FY2027</span><span class=\"track\"><span class=\"fill\" style=\"width:0.15%\"></span></span><span class=\"val\">1.70</span></div>\n      <div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"yr\">FY2028</span><span class=\"track\"><span class=\"fill\" style=\"width:2.5%\"></span></span><span class=\"val\">27.82</span></div>\n  <div class=\"chart\">\n    <p class=\"ch-title\">Original analysis &middot; revenue mix by segment</p>\n    <p class=\"ch-sub\">Why gross margin travels from 39.7% to 87.4%: the plan is not one business growing, it is four businesses changing places. Built from the model&rsquo;s Revenue Build, segment B.</p>\n    <div class=\"mix\">\n      <span class=\"yr\">FY2027<small>&#8377;1.7 Cr</small></span>\n      <span class=\"stack\"><span class=\"seg s-sys\" style=\"width:7.4%\"></span><span class=\"seg s-sen\" style=\"width:22.1%\">22%</span><span class=\"seg s-rob\" style=\"width:70.6%\">Robotics 71%</span></span>\n      <span class=\"yr\">FY2029<small>&#8377;115.4 Cr</small></span>\n      <span class=\"stack\"><span class=\"seg s-sys\" style=\"width:85.9%\">Systems 86%</span><span class=\"seg s-sen\" style=\"width:3.4%\"></span><span class=\"seg s-sem\" style=\"width:4.5%\"></span><span class=\"seg s-rob\" style=\"width:6.2%\"></span></span>\n      <span class=\"yr\">FY2032<small>&#8377;1,128.5 Cr</small></span>\n      <span class=\"stack\"><span class=\"seg s-sys\" style=\"width:83.4%\">Systems 83%</span><span class=\"seg s-sen\" style=\"width:3.0%\"></span><span class=\"seg s-sem\" style=\"width:9.2%\">9%</span><span class=\"seg s-rob\" style=\"width:4.4%\"></span></span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"mix-key\"><span><i class=\"s-sys\" style=\"background:var(--teal)\"></i>Systems</span><span><i style=\"background:var(--copper-fill)\"></i>Sensors</span><span><i style=\"background:var(--ink)\"></i>Semiconductors</span><span><i style=\"background:var(--flag)\"></i>Robotics / defence</span></div>\n    <p class=\"ch-note\">The first bar is the finding. <b>FY2027 is 71% robotics &mdash; effectively one defence line &mdash; and 0% semiconductors.</b> The margin story depends entirely on semiconductors reaching 9.2% of revenue by FY2032, which is the bar that does not exist yet.</p>\n  </div>\n\n      <div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"yr\">FY2029</span><span class=\"track\"><span class=\"fill\" style=\"width:10.2%\"></span></span><span class=\"val\">115.38</span></div>\n      <div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"yr\">FY2030</span><span class=\"track\"><span class=\"fill\" style=\"width:25.2%\"></span></span><span class=\"val\">284.66</span></div>\n      <div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"yr\">FY2031</span><span class=\"track\"><span class=\"fill\" style=\"width:52.7%\"></span></span><span class=\"val\">594.30</span></div>\n      <div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"yr\">FY2032</span><span class=\"track\"><span class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></span></span><span class=\"val\">1,128.45</span></div>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"ramp-foot\">EBITDA positive in FY2028 &middot; gross margin 39.7% &rarr; 87.4% as mix shifts to silicon &middot; prices held flat all six years, so growth is volume only</p>\n  </div>\n  <figure class=\"plate\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"./images/figure-12.webp\" width=\"1600\" height=\"517\" alt=\"Three stacked bar charts of revenue by business line, product category and revenue type from FY2027 to FY2032\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n  <figcaption><span class=\"figno\">Figure 12</span>The company&rsquo;s own three cuts of the same ramp &mdash; by business line, by product category, and by revenue type. <b>These charts total &#8377;1,388 Cr, not &#8377;1,128 Cr</b>; the gap is the eleven product lines carried in the business plan but absent from the model&rsquo;s demand sizing.<span class=\"figsrc\">Source &middot; Information Memorandum, p.23 &mdash; reproduced, not redrawn</span></figcaption></figure>\n  <p>Volume and margin sit in different places, and that is the useful thing to hold onto. <strong>Systems are 83% of revenue</strong>, so group economics track systems. But the marginal rupee is worth most in semiconductors at <strong>94% gross margin</strong>, and those lines need no installer, no warranty logistics and no fitment channel.</p>\n</section><section>\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">Capital</p>\n  <h2>Released against silicon, not against the forecast</h2>\n  <p>&#8377;55 Cr of blended capital: <strong>&#8377;45 Cr of equity ($4.79M) for 18.07%</strong> at a &#8377;204 Cr pre-money, plus a &#8377;10 Cr collateral-free CGTMSE facility for working capital. Dilution is tied only to the milestone that creates enterprise value. Of the equity, <strong>66% goes to tapeout NRE and IP</strong>, 16% to a 10-FTE engineering team over 18 months, 8% to AIS-162/188 type approval through ARAI/ICAT.</p>\n  <p>The $3.17M of NRE is not one commitment. It is four, and each is a point where the next cheque can be withheld:</p>\n  <ol class=\"gates\">\n    <li><span class=\"what\"><b>Prove the blocks on a shared MPW</b>Compute and radar DSP blocks, 5&nbsp;mm&sup2; each, 100 samples</span><span class=\"cost\">$138K</span></li>\n    <li><span class=\"what\"><b>Full-die MPW prototype</b>The complete 57&nbsp;mm&sup2; part plus five prototype wafers</span><span class=\"cost\">$232K</span></li>\n    <li><span class=\"what\"><b>Backend to GDSII</b>Physical design, DFT, integration and sign-off &mdash; only after the blocks work</span><span class=\"cost\">$1.00M</span></li>\n    <li class=\"terminal\"><span class=\"what\"><b>Dedicated production mask</b>The largest single commitment, paid only once silicon exists</span><span class=\"cost\">$1.00M</span></li>\n  </ol>\n  <p>Controller and PHY IP take the remaining $0.8M. At volume the die costs <strong>$3.88</strong> &mdash; $2.38 of wafer against 1,010 good die per 300&nbsp;mm wafer, plus $1.50 of assembly and test. <strong>NRE breaks even at 174,908 chips</strong> against a plan that ships ~217,000 dies through FY2032, and the mask is cut for a ~500,000-die lifetime, which is the volume commitment that earns the $2,400 wafer price the whole cost stack depends on.</p>\n  <figure class=\"plate\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"./images/figure-13.webp\" width=\"1000\" height=\"1033\" alt=\"Four-stage 18-month milestone plan from MPW submission through to Series A readiness\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n  <figcaption><span class=\"figno\">Figure 13</span>What the money buys, month by month. <b>First silicon returns in months 6&ndash;12</b>; ASIC commercial revenue and the Series A trigger sit at month 18.<span class=\"figsrc\">Source &middot; Information Memorandum, p.26 &mdash; reproduced, not redrawn</span></figcaption></figure>\n  <p>The downside case is the one worth reading. At a <strong>70% revenue miss</strong> &mdash; the mandate slips and the pilots are not the market &mdash; the plan still reaches roughly &#8377;339 Cr and self-funds. That is the argument for underwriting the silicon rather than the forecast.</p>\n</section><section>\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">Underwriting</p>\n  <h2>Ten things to test, and where the documents disagree with each other</h2>\n  <p>The materials argue their own risks rather than burying them, which is worth crediting. Three of the ten come from the company&rsquo;s own claim-control ledger, and two are dated cash calls that appear in no allocation line &mdash; it already knows which headline numbers will not survive diligence, which is a good sign about the team and a bad sign about the memorandum. Ordered by what an investor acts on first.</p>\n  <div class=\"rk-legend\">\n    <div><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"t\">Structural &mdash; inherent to the plan&rsquo;s shape, priceable but not fixable</span></div>\n    <div><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"t\">Claim control &mdash; barred by the company&rsquo;s own ledger, printed anyway</span></div>\n    <div><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"t\">Document &mdash; two numbers for one thing, fixable before the data room</span></div>\n    <div><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"t\">Unfunded &mdash; a dated cash call in no allocation line</span></div>\n  </div>\n  <details class=\"risk\">\n    <summary><span class=\"chip\">Structural</span><span class=\"rt\">Concentration &mdash; two products carry 64% of revenue</span><span class=\"smark\"></span></summary>\n    <div class=\"rbody\"><p>The truck kit (&#8377;450 Cr, 40%) and the smart mirror (&#8377;270 Cr, 24%) are the same family sold to overlapping buyers. A certification delay or a fitment bottleneck hits <strong>&#8377;720 Cr at once</strong> &mdash; more than the other thirteen lines combined.</p></div>\n  </details>\n  <details class=\"risk\">\n    <summary><span class=\"chip\">Structural</span><span class=\"rt\">The FPGA window, not the ASIC, is what the next two years are made of</span><span class=\"smark\"></span></summary>\n    <div class=\"rbody\"><p>Qualified volume silicon lands <strong>H1 2028 &mdash; after the all-models date</strong> &mdash; and OEM design-in runs 18 to 30 months. So line-fit revenue cannot come first, and every rupee before H1 2028 has to come from the FPGA module through government and PSU channels (UC-06). The plan&rsquo;s own FY2027 line agrees: &#8377;1.7 Cr, FPGA only. An investor should underwrite the FPGA window explicitly rather than treating it as a run-up to the real business.</p></div>\n  </details>\n  <details class=\"risk\">\n    <summary><span class=\"chip\">Unfunded</span><span class=\"rt\">Fifteen provisional patents expire in March 2027 and nothing pays to convert them</span><span class=\"smark\"></span></summary>\n    <div class=\"rbody\"><p>The provisionals were filed March 2026 (IN2026/DGR/001&ndash;015) and must become complete specifications within twelve months of the priority date. The memorandum lists that expiry among its own four reasons to move &mdash; and then allocates nothing to it. <strong>This is a hard, dated cash call on the IP the entire thesis rests on</strong>, landing inside the round&rsquo;s first year, and it appears in no line of the use of funds.</p></div>\n  </details>\n  <details class=\"risk\">\n    <summary><span class=\"chip\">Unfunded</span><span class=\"rt\">The ISO 26262 assessor gates the highest-value lane and is not in the budget</span><span class=\"smark\"></span></summary>\n    <div class=\"rbody\"><p>No functional-safety pathway is published, and until an assessor is engaged a Tier-1 is comparing a certified incumbent with an uncertified newcomer &mdash; a gap no perception result closes. The company&rsquo;s own 30-day plan lists engaging one as a procurement action, but the use of funds carries <strong>AIS-162/188 type approval only</strong>. Ask for the quote and the line item before the term sheet, not after.</p></div>\n  </details>\n  <details class=\"risk\">\n    <summary><span class=\"chip\">Claim control</span><span class=\"rt\">Three regulatory timelines are in circulation, and only one survives</span><span class=\"smark\"></span></summary>\n    <div class=\"rbody\"><p>The memorandum and the financial model both anchor demand to <strong>GSR 184(E) from April 2026</strong>. The company&rsquo;s own claim controls list &ldquo;an April 2026 mandate&rdquo; and &ldquo;GSR 184(E) as final law&rdquo; as <em>banned claims</em>, and the standards-level dates are 2027&ndash;2028. This is not pedantry: it moves first mandated revenue by roughly eighteen months, and it is the first thing a diligence team with a regulatory adviser will check.</p></div>\n  </details>\n  <details class=\"risk\">\n    <summary><span class=\"chip\">Claim control</span><span class=\"rt\">The &#8377;1 Cr defence-revenue claim does not survive its own claim controls</span><span class=\"smark\"></span></summary>\n    <div class=\"rbody\"><p>It appears on the memorandum cover and in the model&rsquo;s historical context. The internal ledger substantiates <strong>&#8377;23.01L delivered</strong> and <strong>&#8377;78.39L at L1 stage &mdash; lowest bidder, not an award</strong> &mdash; sitting in a different legal entity (Deepgrid Datacentre Pvt Ltd) with the IP owned by MCEME. The delivered revenue is real and is genuine proof the stack works before silicon; the headline is not the number to put in front of an investor.</p></div>\n  </details>\n  <details class=\"risk\">\n    <summary><span class=\"chip\">Document</span><span class=\"rt\">The two totals in circulation are &#8377;1,128 Cr and &#8377;1,388 Cr</span><span class=\"smark\"></span></summary>\n    <div class=\"rbody\"><p>They differ by <strong>&#8377;259.5 Cr</strong> across eleven product lines that the business plan carries and the financial model does not size. This is not only a document-to-document gap: the information memorandum&rsquo;s own revenue slide is <em>headed</em> &#8377;1,128 Cr while its tables sum to &#8377;1,388 Cr. Pick one before the data room opens; the model is the conservative document and the one this summary follows.</p></div>\n  </details>\n  <details class=\"risk\">\n    <summary><span class=\"chip\">Document</span><span class=\"rt\">Tapeout NRE is quoted at both $2.42M and $3.17M</span><span class=\"smark\"></span></summary>\n    <div class=\"rbody\"><p>The die card says $2.42M; the platform slide says &ldquo;a single $3.17M tapeout&rdquo;; the model&rsquo;s use-of-funds says $3.17M phased across four gates. A <strong>$750K difference in the single largest line item</strong> is the first thing a diligence team will price. Same for the addressable pool &mdash; 5M+ trucks in the memorandum against 1.0M in the model.</p></div>\n  </details>\n  <details class=\"risk\">\n    <summary><span class=\"chip\">Claim control</span><span class=\"rt\">The compute-box line should not be underwritten on price</span><span class=\"smark\"></span></summary>\n    <div class=\"rbody\"><p>Published module pricing for embedded edge-AI parts does not support a price-advantage claim for the A100 SKUs, several of which carry fewer channels than comparably priced alternatives. The defensible positions are <strong>domestic supply, India-tuned perception and deployed-system cost</strong> &mdash; and a like-for-like deployed comparison is a diligence deliverable, not a slide. The company&rsquo;s own claim controls bar quoting any competitor per-unit price, which the memorandum&rsquo;s pricing slide does anyway.</p></div>\n  </details>\n  <details class=\"risk\">\n    <summary><span class=\"chip\">Structural</span><span class=\"rt\">Key-person exposure on both sides of the company</span><span class=\"smark\"></span></summary>\n    <div class=\"rbody\"><p>The founder is the single point of commercial accountability across all four business units and holds 95.6% of shares. The CTO &mdash; architect of the matrix ALU and author of the radar RTL &mdash; <strong>is not yet full-time</strong>, with the plan showing Q1 FY28. Separately, the cap table totals 102,797 shares against the 100,890 used in the pricing basis, a 1,907-share difference to reconcile before term sheet.</p></div>\n  </details>\n\n  <p>Two things that were flagged earlier and now resolve cleanly. The <strong>&ldquo;six cameras&rdquo; versus &ldquo;eleven channels&rdquo;</strong> question is a difference of scope, not an error: the AD2 kit is specified at six cameras, and the compute box ingests eleven channels (7 RGB + 2 thermal + 2 radar) in the same 8.6&nbsp;ms. And <strong>prior capital is deployed, not banked</strong>: &#8377;48 lakh of grants (ARAI &#8377;36L, HDFC Parivartan &#8377;12L) and ~&#8377;2 Cr of angel funding are fully spent, which is why the &#8377;2.5 lakh cash position is a date, not a number.</p>\n</section>\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"close\">\n  <blockquote>&ldquo;The portfolio is not fifteen bets. It is one bet, fifteen times over.&rdquo;</blockquote>\n  <p>Release capital against silicon, certification and paying customers &mdash; the four tapeout gates are already structured as tranches, and six of the nine de-risking milestones are marked done before the round opens. The forecast is the consequence of those gates, not the thing being funded.</p>\n  <p class=\"src\">Sources &middot; Deepgrid Semi Pre-Series A Information Memorandum, June 2026 (33 pp) &middot; Deepgrid_Semi_Financial_Model_Corrected_v3-sept.xlsx &mdash; P&amp;L, Revenue Build, Tapeout Unit Economics, Use of Funds, Demand &amp; TAM, Assumptions &middot; 104-slide product portfolio deck &middot; NVIDIA Jetson published module pricing<br>Figures are management projections prepared for fundraising, not audited. Images reproduced from the information memorandum.</p>\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n";
